{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgke1bTF3R3EGv2fhfTwV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SwtLXJFv3h7cu8qS4dqLBX","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162033__x07393c/work/PLAN.md","offset":600,"limit":250},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9038,"cache_read_input_tokens":44034,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9038},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"feff64bd-df6d-45b2-b337-83604d3a2d73","uuid":"dc5a6b98-63c2-4499-b7d7-19c51b080429","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:20:49.314Z","request_id":"req_011Cgke1bD7KCfh7wh49KMbR","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01SwtLXJFv3h7cu8qS4dqLBX":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162033__x07393c/work/PLAN.md","offset":600,"limit":250}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SwtLXJFv3h7cu8qS4dqLBX","type":"tool_result","content":"600\t          {do:'report',to:'vance',text:'REPORT TO VANCE'} ],\n601\t  onDone:[ {burnStrip:'A'}, {ledger:{paid:15}} ] }\n602\t```\n603\t**Step types:** `goto leave talk report use deliver destroy kill collect steal hold escort ride timer choice script`. A step shows its `text` for 5 s at the top when it starts, and always in the map margin. Bots drive these same steps.\n604\t\n605\tContracts are taken in person (a short FP scene: the camera holds on the giver, subtitles, then Accept or Not Yet) or through the notice board in Mile Forty. After M2, the order within M3/M4 and M5/M6 is free; M5 needs M3 and M6 needs M4 (one faction's path each); M7 needs all four. Acts, for the fever's pace: act 1 is M0 to M2, act 2 is M3 to M6, act 3 is M7 onward.\n606\t\n607\t| # | Title (giver) | Length, time | What happens | Teaches | Alternate plan | Consequence, pay |\n608\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n609\t| M0 | The Goods Line | 2 min, dusk, skippable | You ride Old Bakr's flatcar into the Kettle as he talks. Prompt: raise the map (must do). The margin note. Fever on the platform; you fall | Look, map | - | Fade to the clinic |\n610\t| M1 | Mercy Run (Odile) | 7 min, morning | Wake at the clinic. Take a tablet. Given an old `tractor` (cond 45). Drive medicine to Three Wells. On the way back P2 is manned. The 5th shot **jams by script**; then the truck is hit and stalls: repair. Syrette. Report | Walk, use, tablet, drive, waypoint, fire, jam, reload, syrette, repair | - | +3 tablets, 5 stones, Pump Shed |\n611\t| M2 | A Cage at the Post (Tibor) | 7 min, best at night | Ines owes Tibor. She's in a cage at Ranger Post (8 Concord, a tower). Scout with the monocular, cross in grass, cane knife, or go loud. Open the cage (hold). Ines fights her way out with you. She explains rescues by doing one if you fall | Monocular, stealth, melee, sleep to choose the hour, safehouse capture, buddy | - | Ranger Post safehouse, 8 stones, Ines |\n612\t| M3 | Fuel for the Peace (Vance) | 7 min | Burn the Harvest's 3 tanks at East Siding. Vance hands you the flare pistol. Wind pinned toward the depot: the grass will carry fire if you start it upwind | Flare, wind, fire, chain explosions | Ines: steal the tanker at P3 and drive it in; soldiers hold fire until you're inside | Scar A, 15 stones (+5). A column of smoke visible across the map for a game day |\n613\t| M4 | Seed Money (Ansa) | 7 min | Payroll convoy (2 technicals, a truck) crosses the Salt Pan on a loop. Stop it, take the case. It flies out when the truck blows: you get the tracker to find it in the salt | Vehicle combat, MG, tracker | Dov: plant his charges on the bridge, detonate as the convoy crosses | 20 stones (+5), tracker, Dov |\n614\t| M5 | The Water Question (Vance) | 7 min | Destroy the pump on the Mercy, because Three Wells \"feeds the Harvest\" | Charges, defending, moral cost | Mags: first open the bypass and hold the pump house for 60 s, so the cistern fills | Without alt: Three Wells empties, a line of people walks the road to the clinic, its huts go dark, Odile refuses tablets until you do a Mercy Run free. With alt: village stays, pay 10 instead of 20 |\n615\t| M6 | The Long Field (Ansa) | 9 min, forced night | Burn the Concord's crop and its ammo bunker. Your highest-trust buddy comes along (with no buddy alive, a Harvest guide named Pell does). At about 70% the wind turns (scripted) and they go down on fire: **Syrette or Finish It** | Night fire, buddy choice | The mission itself | Scar B, 25 stones, the Ledger's first hard line |\n616\t| M7 | The Cut (Harrow's note) | 10 min | A note at your safehouse: *You have drawn well. Come and see.* Truce collapses: both armies fight for the mine. Reach the sluice house through crossfire and wildfire, take his ledger. In it: *One contractor, paid in advance, to walk the Kettle.* Signed by him | Three-way fight, technical MG, big fire | A surviving buddy calls: they hold the east road if you go in from the pit side (no bonus stones, +1 trust) | Scar C. Truce over: Mile Forty loses its no-fire zone, Tibor moves his stock into safehouse lockers. Act 2 fever pace |\n617\t| M8 | Last Train (Odile) | 7 min | Mile Forty under shells. Hold the platform 120 s while people board. Then ride Old Bakr's train to East Siding on a flatcar MG, 60 s, on rails, under fire. *He says the grass won't burn twice.* The column starts walking the scar | Defence, on-rails MG | - | Column on the map, moving slowly and visibly along the scar |\n618\t| M9 | The Surveyor | 10 min, night, storm | Climb to the Observatory (deserters from both armies; no fires, it's raining). Harrow sits at a table with a lamp, as sick as you. The scene: he lays your contract map down; the three scars glow as one line; he draws the last stroke. He offers tablets and the minefield sheet, and asks you to finish your contract, or not | Choice | - | `choice` steps: shoot him or don't (a Ledger line, no other effect). Then who gets the sheet |\n619\t| End | The Pass | 3 to 4 min | Either walk to the Pass alone, or take the sheet to the column and hold behind them. Surviving buddies arrive (200 HP, real AI, last lines), with pursuit from both armies. Rain stops. The last grass is yours to light | Everything | - | Ending card, Ledger, credits, title. Continue returns to the last safehouse for free roam |\n620\t\n621\t**Story scars.** On completing M3, M6 and M7, call `burnStrip('A'|'B'|'C')` so the arc exists whatever the player actually burned: A from East Siding west to the Cut, C across the Cut, B from the Cut west through the Long Field to the Pass road. The player sees it first in M9.\n622\t\n623\t**Ending cards:**\n624\t- **Walk out:** *You reached the border with a case of stones and a map nobody else will ever use. The guard asks your trade. You tell him: surveyor.*\n625\t- **Give it to them:** *They crossed at first light, walking on ash. Nobody has asked who lit it. The fever is not finished with you, and you are out of tablets. It is a good view.*\n626\t\n627\t**Attract, tests and dev mode** can jump to any mission start: each mission has a `setup` that puts the world in the right state (`world.reset`, story flags, scars, buddies, loadout), so `dev.startMission('m6')` is one call.\n628\t\n629\t---\n630\t\n631\t## 15. Writing\n632\t\n633\t**Voice.** Weary, literary and exact. Short declarative sentences. Euphemism as cruelty. Gallows humour without a wink. Nobody explains the theme. Nobody is your friend without a price. People are tired, and they're smart. Think of a war correspondent who stopped filing years ago. Don't quote real authors, and don't imitate the source's lines.\n634\t\n635\tEach mission gets 8 to 15 spoken lines in this voice. Each character has a tic: **Vance** invoices (*conclude, regrettable, the matter of*). **Ansa** corrects grammar. **Odile** counts things. **Tibor** talks about returns. **Bakr** tells you what stations used to be called. **Ines** owes people, or they owe her. **Dov** tells a three-sentence story that ends badly. **Mags** narrates what she is doing to you. **Harrow** writes like a surveyor's notebook.\n636\t\n637\tAll game text must be in the HUD font's character set. Subtitle lines stay under 60 characters, two lines at most: split long sentences across lines in sequence.\n638\t\n639\tUse these lines verbatim, and write the rest to match:\n640\t\n641\t- **Bakr, M0:** *Forty miles of track and not one station that remembers its name.* / *They paint the signs over. Whoever won last.* / *You have the look of a man who read about this place. Reading is a good way to visit.* / *Up there they will ask you which side. Say yes.*\n642\t- **Odile:** *Three tablets. The fourth you pay for. I do not mean in stones.* / *I do not need you to be good. I need you to be on time.* / *Sixty-one beds. Forty blankets. You are the math.*\n643\t- **Vance:** *We do not burn villages. We conclude them.* / *The water question has been a great sorrow to this office.* / *Your invoice will be honoured, regrettably.*\n644\t- **Ansa:** *You said less people. Fewer. Fewer people. It will matter by the end of the month.* / *Burn the field. A hungry man learns to read the wind.*\n645\t- **Tibor:** *Everything on this rack has been returned at least once.* / *It fires. If you want it to fire twice, that is a different price.*\n646\t- **Ines:** *I flew for both of them. Neither paid. Get in.* / *You owe me a truck. You owe me several trucks.*\n647\t- **Dov:** *Two fingers I left in this country. I came back to see what they are doing.* / *A man asked me to mine his own road, so he would know where it was safe. He was right for a week.*\n648\t- **Mags:** *Hold still. No, you can't feel that. No, that's normal. Hold still.* / *Not today. Today you owe me money.*\n649\t- **A burning buddy:** *Don't let it be the fire. Please. Not the fire.*\n650\t- **Barks:** *There! In the grass!* / *Who lit that?* / *It's stuck! It's stuck again!* / *Leave him, he's already gone.*\n651\t- **Harrow's margin notes,** one per trig point, in order:\n652\t  1. *A map is a promise made by someone who has already left.*\n653\t  2. *I drew the river where the Company wanted it. The river was slow to comply, but it came round.*\n654\t  3. *Both armies buy from me. The Concord pays on time. The Harvest pays in grain and tears. I have eaten better on the tears.*\n655\t  4. *You will have noticed that you follow roads. I drew those too.*\n656\t  5. *Grass is the only honest border. It goes where the wind tells it, and it keeps a record.*\n657\t  6. *By now you have burned what I marked. Look at it from the ridge. Tell me that is not a line.*\n658\t- **Harrow, M9:** *You are late. I said you would be. Sit down, it won't take long, neither of us has long.* / *I drew the lines that started this. I would like to draw one more.* / *You have been drawing for me. Look at it.* / *Burned grass cannot burn twice. It is the only safe road in the country, and you built it for wages.*\n659\t- **Load-screen epigraphs** (*from Harrow's field notes*): write 12 in the same voice.\n660\t\n661\t---\n662\t\n663\t## 16. UI and UX\n664\t\n665\t**10-foot and controller first.** A PS5 DualSense on a TV at ten feet is the design target. Mouse and keyboard play the same game on the same screens and feel native. Everything is drawn with `ctx.hud` in art pixels; there is no DOM UI at all, so it all works in Node tests. Test the view at 1920×1080.\n666\t\n667\t**Layout rules:**\n668\t- Safe area 24 px horizontal, 14 px vertical.\n669\t- Menu items at scale 2; the smallest text anywhere is scale 1 (subtitles, prompts).\n670\t- At most 6 items on a screen, one idea per screen.\n671\t- No tables, no scroll lists, no web-style data screens. Long content is paged.\n672\t- A focused item has a full-width bar in `orange` and a small marker. Move and confirm sounds.\n673\t- Only the title and pause menus cover the view. Every other screen is in your hands or an overlay with the world visible behind it.\n674\t\n675\t**HUD in play is minimal** and hides 6 s after it last changed:\n676\t- 5 health segments, syrette and tablet counts bottom-left.\n677\t- Ammo and the gun's condition icon bottom-right.\n678\t- A dot reticle (hidden while scoped; the scope has its own black mask).\n679\t- Prompts centre-bottom. Subtitles above them with the speaker's name in a colour.\n680\t- Mission step at the top for 5 s when it changes.\n681\t\n682\t**Controls** (`src/core/actions.js`):\n683\t\n684\t| Action | DualSense | Xbox glyph | Keyboard and mouse |\n685\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n686\t| Move / look | L stick / R stick | same | WASD / mouse |\n687\t| Fire / aim | R2 / L2 | RT / LT | LMB / RMB |\n688\t| Use (when a prompt shows), else reload | Square | X | E / R |\n689\t| Jump | Cross | A | Space |\n690\t| Crouch | Circle | B | C (never Ctrl: Ctrl+W closes the browser tab) |\n691\t| Sprint | L3 (click) | LS | Left Shift |\n692\t| Melee | R3 | RS | F |\n693\t| Next weapon | Triangle | Y | Wheel, or 1-4 |\n694\t| Throw / plant | R1 | RB | G |\n695\t| Syrette, surgery | L1 | LB | Q |\n696\t| Map up / down | D-pad Up | D-pad Up | M or Tab |\n697\t| Tablet | D-pad Down | D-pad Down | H |\n698\t| Tracker | D-pad Left | D-pad Left | T |\n699\t| Monocular (hold) | D-pad Right | D-pad Right | V |\n700\t| Pause | Options | Menu | Esc |\n701\t| Ledger | Create | View | J |\n702\t| **Driving:** gas / brake-reverse / steer | R2 / L2 / L stick | RT / LT / L stick | W / S / A-D |\n703\t| Handbrake | Cross | A | Space |\n704\t| Get out / repair | Square | X | E |\n705\t| Swap to gun | Triangle | Y | F |\n706\t| Chase camera | R3 | RS | C |\n707\t\n708\tUse `input.preventKeys.add('Tab')` etc. Analog triggers: each frame, read `navigator.getGamepads()` buttons 6 and 7 `value` and `input.send({ tr:[l2, r2] })` when changed, so recordings keep it, and use it for throttle and brake. Rumble: `pad.vibrationActuator?.playEffect('dual-rumble', {...})`, guarded, Settings toggle.\n709\t\n710\t**Glyphs.** Prompts follow the input used last:\n711\t- `device` flips to `kbm` on keydown, mouse button or real mouse movement, and to `pad` on any `Pad*` code or a stick past 0.35.\n712\t- `src/ui/glyphs.js` is pixel art as `hud.sprite` rows, about 11 × 11: Cross, Circle, Square, Triangle, L1, L2, R1, R2, L3, R3, D-pad directions, Options, Create; Xbox A, B, X, Y, LB, LT, RB, RT, LS, RS, Menu, View; a key cap drawn around any letter; LMB, RMB, MMB, wheel.\n713\t- Settings has **Glyphs: PlayStation / Xbox**, default PlayStation.\n714\t- `game.state().prompts` lists what's on screen, so tests can check it.\n715\t\n716\t**The mouse is native.** In menus the pointer is free (no lock), hover moves focus, click activates (read `input.buttonEvents`; convert with `x = (p.x+1)/2*hud.width`, `y = (1-p.y)/2*hud.height`). The wheel scrolls pages. Over the world it aims and looks under pointer lock. On the held map it's a cursor (hover focuses a marker, click sets the waypoint). On Tibor's rack and in dialogue choices, click works too. Keyboard in menus: arrows or WASD, Enter or Space, Esc back. Pad in menus: D-pad or left stick with key repeat, Cross confirms, Circle goes back, L1/R1 change tabs and pages. If the pad disconnects during play, open the pause menu.\n717\t\n718\t**The held map** (`src/world/map-texture.js`). The heart of pillar 3.\n719\t- 320 × 240 DataTexture on a plane about 0.5 × 0.375 m, about 0.42 m in front of the camera, tilted, in both hands (the `hand` model and hands rig), filling about 70% of the width, so one texel is about one art pixel. A 0.62 m plane, which I tried first, was too big.\n720\t- Baked at start: contour lines every 8 m on sand paper, river, roads, rail, labels in your own 5×7 `pixfont.js`.\n721\t- Redrawn at up to 2 Hz on a copy: burn scars (ink), your position and heading, the waypoint, sites you've seen, mission step and Harrow's notes in the margin, wind arrow and clock on a small GPS clipped to the corner.\n722\t- Raise and lower takes 0.4 s with paper sound. **The world never stops.** You can walk and drive with it up. While it's up, the look input moves the map cursor.\n723\t- Square/LMB on a marker sets the waypoint; Triangle or wheel toggles a closer zoom.\n724\t- It works at night because the paper uses a dim lit toon plus a small hand torch `lights.request` following the view group.\n725\t\n726\t**Screens:**\n727\t- **Loading:** the engine's, then a black screen with one Harrow epigraph.\n728\t- **Title:** live 3D scene (dusk, fixed slow camera over burning grass on the Long Field, music), the title large (scale 4, or 3 if it won't fit), the latest input's *Press [glyph]*. Then the main menu.\n729\t- **Main menu:** Continue (when a save exists), New Game, Cash Run, Settings, About and Credits.\n730\t- **Pause** (`timeScale = 0`): Resume, Ledger, Settings, Dev Mode, About and Credits, Quit to Title. In a hub session: Resume and Settings only.\n731\t- **Settings:** Sound (Music slider **default 10%**, Effects, Voices), Controls (Look sensitivity for pad, for mouse; Invert Y; Aim assist; Rumble; Glyphs), Picture (Fullscreen, for the TV; Pixel size Fine/Chunky via `engine.settings.set`; Quality; Field of view), Comfort (Subtitle size; Reduce flashes; Fever effects reduced), Reset to Defaults. Saved in your own `localStorage` entry and re-applied at boot: `settings:{ button:false, key:false }` hides the engine's panel and stops the engine saving its own copy.\n732\t- **Dialogue:** the camera holds on the speaker; subtitles; two big buttons at most.\n733\t- **Tibor's rack:** one gun at a time, large (its first-person model turned to the side on a table), name, three bars (Damage, Range, Reliability), price. Left/right cycles. Buy or Take.\n734\t- **Locker:** one row per slot, left/right picks.\n735\t- **Bed:** Dawn, Noon, Dusk, Midnight, Leave.\n736\t- **Ledger:** section 13.\n737\t- **Game Over, Ending card, Credits.**\n738\t- **About and Credits:** paged, see section 27.\n739\t\n740\t**Touch-only devices.** Detect with `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches` and no pad connected (verified: true on Chromium with the `iPhone 14`, `iPad Pro 11` and `Pixel 7` profiles, false on a desktop context). Engine option `touch:false` always, so there are never on-screen controls. On such a device the title shows **Controller or keyboard required** (the exact text in `state().notice`, drawn uppercase by the font) and one large **Settings** button (tap works as click: `input.buttonEvents` reports a finger as code `Touch`). Attract mode still starts after 10 s; a tap exits to this screen. A key press or pad connecting clears the gate and shows the normal title.\n741\t\n742\t---\n743\t\n744\t## 17. Dev mode\n745\t\n746\tPause menu → **Dev Mode** (hidden in a hub session). An overlay with tabs (L1/R1 or Q/E), world visible behind, playing or frozen by a toggle.\n747\t\n748\t| Tab | Contents |\n749\t| --- | --- |\n750\t| Cheats | God mode, infinite ammo, no jams, no fever, invisible to AI, noclip fly |\n751\t| Teleport | Every site, every post, every case, the crosshair point |\n752\t| Spawn | Squad of each faction, pickup, technical, truck, a stone case, a buddy |\n753\t| World | Hour slider, wind direction and speed sliders, weather (clear, dust, storm), ignite at crosshair, extinguish all, regrow all, sleep +6 h |\n754\t| Mission | Start any mission, complete current step, set story flags, give stones, tablets, syrettes, all guns; break gun; force jam; force fever; down a buddy |\n755\t| **Balance** | Live sliders (below), **Reset to Defaults** for all, Square/R resets one |\n756\t| Debug | Fire-grid overlay, nav overlay, AI state text over heads, counts (actors, burning cells, draw info from `engine.state()`), engine debug panel (`engine.showDebug`), free camera (`engine.setCamera({ preset:'free' })`, restored after; re-install `step` in `onCameraChange`), crosshair coordinates for placing things in `src/content/`, Quick Save/Load, show `status()` |\n757\t\n758\t**Balance sliders** (left/right steps, hold accelerates, mouse drags). Defaults in `src/content/tuning-defaults.js`:\n759\t\n760\t| Slider | Default | Range |\n761\t| --- | --- | --- |\n762\t| `playerSpeed` multiplier | 1 | 0.5-2 |\n763\t| `playerDamageTaken` multiplier | 1 | 0-3 |\n764\t| `weaponDamage` multiplier | 1 | 0.25-4 |\n765\t| `enemyHealth` multiplier | 1 | 0.25-4 |\n766\t| `enemyAccuracy` | 1 | 0.25-3 |\n767\t| `enemyVision` (m) | 90 | 20-200 |\n768\t| `enemyReaction` (s) | 0.45 | 0.1-2 |\n769\t| `wearRate` | 1 | 0-5 |\n770\t| `jamRate` | 1 | 0-5 |\n771\t| `fireSpread` | 1 | 0-3 |\n772\t| `fireDamage` (HP/s) | 8 | 0-30 |\n773\t| `windEffect` | 1 | 0-3 |\n774\t| `feverMinutes` | 12 | 2-40 |\n775\t| `vehicleTopSpeed` (m/s) | 26 | 10-45 |\n776\t| `vehicleToughness` | 1 | 0.25-4 |\n777\t| `stonesReward` multiplier | 1 | 0-5 |\n778\t| `buddyWoundChance` | 0.15 | 0-1 |\n779\t| `dayMinutes` | 30 | 2-120 |\n780\t| `postRemanHours` | 24 | 1-96 |\n781\t| `regrowHours` | 48 | 1-200 |\n782\t\n783\tA test sets every slider, checks the system responds, presses Reset, and checks every value equals its default.\n784\t\n785\t---\n786\t\n787\t## 18. Attract mode\n788\t\n789\tAfter **10 seconds with no input on the title screen or main menu**, start a looping demo (`src/attract/`). Settings and About are exempt, because people stop to read them. It's a director with a list of beats, using the real game with `cam.override`, god mode, infinite ammo and bot input through the same action layer. It cheats freely: teleports, spawns, sets the hour and wind. A `save.disabled` flag stops it touching saves.\n790\t\n791\tBeats (10 to 14 s each, joined by `engine.screen.cover('dither')` and `reveal`), to show as much as possible:\n792\t1. Dusk, driving a technical down the road, first person, raising the map at the wheel.\n793\t2. Rolling into a checkpoint, gunfight, the gun jams, slap and rack.\n794\t3. Flare into dry grass, the wind takes it, soldiers run burning.\n795\t4. Night, the Long Field in flames, chase camera past it.\n796\t5. Fever: the view swims, tablet to mouth.\n797\t6. Field surgery with pliers.\n798\t7. Scoped shot from a ridge at noon.\n799\t8. Dragged out by a buddy; syrette or finish it.\n800\t9. Tracker beeping to a case in a burnt wreck.\n801\t10. Train with the flatcar MG.\n802\t11. Tibor's rack, a line of his.\n803\t12. The map on a table with the scars glowing.\n804\t13. The title.\n805\t\n806\tHUD shows a `DEMO` tag and *Press [glyph]*. **Any input exits** (key, mouse button or real movement, pad button or stick, tap) back to the screen it came from, after `world.reset()`. The loop must run indefinitely without error. It runs behind the touch gate too. Never in a hub session.\n807\t\n808\t---\n809\t\n810\t## 19. Multiplayer\n811\t\n812\tFollow the AI Hub Session Protocol v1 (read `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`; also the shared-world example `examples/arena.html` beside it). The hub runs invites, lobby, names, clock and results; the game runs the round. The same code also plays when the game is on its own.\n813\t\n814\t**Mode: `shared-world`, 1 to 4 players.** Four mercs in one burning valley, friends until the stones are counted.\n815\t\n816\t**The round, \"Cash Run\" (6 minutes):**\n817\t- The valley around the Cut: the campaign's terrain, with only the Cut, P5 and the Ranger Post live, 16 to 24 soldiers, wind and fire on.\n818\t- Six stone cases in guarded spots, shown by the tracker's beep and a marker when close. One extraction truck on the road south of the pit.\n819\t- Everyone starts at a different road end with `tractor` (cond 70), `flare`, `cane`, 2 syrettes, 2 bottles.\n820\t- Carry one case at a time (speed × 0.85, you can't sprint); walk it to the truck to bank its stones. Most stones wins.\n821\t- Down at 0 HP: you drop the case and bleed for 25 s. Another player can hold Use for 3 s to bring you up (+1 Revive) or just take the case. Bleed out and you return at your road end after 15 s. Friendly fire is on: that's the theme.\n822\t- On foot only, in rounds: no player vehicles.\n823\t- Ends when the time is up, or when all cases are banked or burned. Standings by stones, ties together.\n824\t\n825\t**Session head tags** go in the template (section 23): `hub:session` 1, `hub:session-players` `1-4`, `hub:session-mode` `shared-world`, `hub:session-minutes` `6`, `hub:webgpu` `required`, `hub:session-goal` *Carry the most diamond cases out of the burning mine*, `hub:session-howto` *Stick/WASD move, R2/mouse fire, Square/E use, carry cases to the truck*.\n826\t\n827\t**Boot order** (`src/main.js`). This is the part that makes the hub work:\n828\t```js\n829\tconst info = (window.AIHub && AIHub.active) ? await AIHub.connect({ mode:'shared-world', seats:[1,4], card:true }) : null;\n830\tif (info) {\n831\t  const game = createGame({ session: hubSession(info) });        // mode 'round': no title, no menus, no attract\n832\t  if (info.server) { const e = await Engine.headless(game, {}); AIHub.ready(); setInterval(() => e.step(6, 1/60), 100); }\n833\t  else if (!navigator.gpu) AIHub.fail('This game needs WebGPU');\n834\t  else await Engine.start(game, { ...OPTIONS, seed: info.seed });  // game.ready(ctx) calls AIHub.ready() once, with no key press\n835\t} else { /* normal start: touch check, title */ }\n836\t```\n837\tHandle a rejected `__PIXEL_READY__` by `AIHub.fail(message)`. If `connect` answers `null`, run as on your own.\n838\t\n839\t**`src/net/session.js`:** one interface, three implementations, so round code never knows which: `{ kind, me, players:[{id,name,color}], host, isHost, server, time(), rng(label), send(data,{to,reliable}), on(event,fn), ready(), answer(what), finish(outcome), fail(msg) }`.\n840\t- `hubSession` wraps `AIHub`.\n841\t- `soloSession` is **on its own**: host is you, the other seats are AI mercs (reuse the buddy brain: go to the nearest case, bank it, shoot what shoots you), with your own results screen at the end.\n842\t- `linkSession` is **on its own with a friend on the same computer**: `BroadcastChannel('game-link-v1')` between two windows. Host and Join on the Cash Run menu, a simple lobby, `start` carrying a `Date.now()` time base and a seed. It costs little, reuses everything, and is how two-window play gets tested.\n843\t\n844\tThe main menu's Cash Run offers: Solo with Hired Guns, Host on This Computer, Join on This Computer, plus one line saying friends online play through AI Hub.\n845\t\n846\t**Netcode.** The host runs the world. Each copy moves its own player from its own stick, at once, never waiting for the network, as `arena.html` does.\n847\t\n848\t| Message | Direction | Rate, kind | Content |\n849\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"feff64bd-df6d-45b2-b337-83604d3a2d73","uuid":"75ec7e51-3298-41b1-a904-9d720187e16b","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:20:49.320Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162033__x07393c/work/PLAN.md","content":"          {do:'report',to:'vance',text:'REPORT TO VANCE'} ],\n  onDone:[ {burnStrip:'A'}, {ledger:{paid:15}} ] }\n```\n**Step types:** `goto leave talk report use deliver destroy kill collect steal hold escort ride timer choice script`. A step shows its `text` for 5 s at the top when it starts, and always in the map margin. Bots drive these same steps.\n\nContracts are taken in person (a short FP scene: the camera holds on the giver, subtitles, then Accept or Not Yet) or through the notice board in Mile Forty. After M2, the order within M3/M4 and M5/M6 is free; M5 needs M3 and M6 needs M4 (one faction's path each); M7 needs all four. Acts, for the fever's pace: act 1 is M0 to M2, act 2 is M3 to M6, act 3 is M7 onward.\n\n| # | Title (giver) | Length, time | What happens | Teaches | Alternate plan | Consequence, pay |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| M0 | The Goods Line | 2 min, dusk, skippable | You ride Old Bakr's flatcar into the Kettle as he talks. Prompt: raise the map (must do). The margin note. Fever on the platform; you fall | Look, map | - | Fade to the clinic |\n| M1 | Mercy Run (Odile) | 7 min, morning | Wake at the clinic. Take a tablet. Given an old `tractor` (cond 45). Drive medicine to Three Wells. On the way back P2 is manned. The 5th shot **jams by script**; then the truck is hit and stalls: repair. Syrette. Report | Walk, use, tablet, drive, waypoint, fire, jam, reload, syrette, repair | - | +3 tablets, 5 stones, Pump Shed |\n| M2 | A Cage at the Post (Tibor) | 7 min, best at night | Ines owes Tibor. She's in a cage at Ranger Post (8 Concord, a tower). Scout with the monocular, cross in grass, cane knife, or go loud. Open the cage (hold). Ines fights her way out with you. She explains rescues by doing one if you fall | Monocular, stealth, melee, sleep to choose the hour, safehouse capture, buddy | - | Ranger Post safehouse, 8 stones, Ines |\n| M3 | Fuel for the Peace (Vance) | 7 min | Burn the Harvest's 3 tanks at East Siding. Vance hands you the flare pistol. Wind pinned toward the depot: the grass will carry fire if you start it upwind | Flare, wind, fire, chain explosions | Ines: steal the tanker at P3 and drive it in; soldiers hold fire until you're inside | Scar A, 15 stones (+5). A column of smoke visible across the map for a game day |\n| M4 | Seed Money (Ansa) | 7 min | Payroll convoy (2 technicals, a truck) crosses the Salt Pan on a loop. Stop it, take the case. It flies out when the truck blows: you get the tracker to find it in the salt | Vehicle combat, MG, tracker | Dov: plant his charges on the bridge, detonate as the convoy crosses | 20 stones (+5), tracker, Dov |\n| M5 | The Water Question (Vance) | 7 min | Destroy the pump on the Mercy, because Three Wells \"feeds the Harvest\" | Charges, defending, moral cost | Mags: first open the bypass and hold the pump house for 60 s, so the cistern fills | Without alt: Three Wells empties, a line of people walks the road to the clinic, its huts go dark, Odile refuses tablets until you do a Mercy Run free. With alt: village stays, pay 10 instead of 20 |\n| M6 | The Long Field (Ansa) | 9 min, forced night | Burn the Concord's crop and its ammo bunker. Your highest-trust buddy comes along (with no buddy alive, a Harvest guide named Pell does). At about 70% the wind turns (scripted) and they go down on fire: **Syrette or Finish It** | Night fire, buddy choice | The mission itself | Scar B, 25 stones, the Ledger's first hard line |\n| M7 | The Cut (Harrow's note) | 10 min | A note at your safehouse: *You have drawn well. Come and see.* Truce collapses: both armies fight for the mine. Reach the sluice house through crossfire and wildfire, take his ledger. In it: *One contractor, paid in advance, to walk the Kettle.* Signed by him | Three-way fight, technical MG, big fire | A surviving buddy calls: they hold the east road if you go in from the pit side (no bonus stones, +1 trust) | Scar C. Truce over: Mile Forty loses its no-fire zone, Tibor moves his stock into safehouse lockers. Act 2 fever pace |\n| M8 | Last Train (Odile) | 7 min | Mile Forty under shells. Hold the platform 120 s while people board. Then ride Old Bakr's train to East Siding on a flatcar MG, 60 s, on rails, under fire. *He says the grass won't burn twice.* The column starts walking the scar | Defence, on-rails MG | - | Column on the map, moving slowly and visibly along the scar |\n| M9 | The Surveyor | 10 min, night, storm | Climb to the Observatory (deserters from both armies; no fires, it's raining). Harrow sits at a table with a lamp, as sick as you. The scene: he lays your contract map down; the three scars glow as one line; he draws the last stroke. He offers tablets and the minefield sheet, and asks you to finish your contract, or not | Choice | - | `choice` steps: shoot him or don't (a Ledger line, no other effect). Then who gets the sheet |\n| End | The Pass | 3 to 4 min | Either walk to the Pass alone, or take the sheet to the column and hold behind them. Surviving buddies arrive (200 HP, real AI, last lines), with pursuit from both armies. Rain stops. The last grass is yours to light | Everything | - | Ending card, Ledger, credits, title. Continue returns to the last safehouse for free roam |\n\n**Story scars.** On completing M3, M6 and M7, call `burnStrip('A'|'B'|'C')` so the arc exists whatever the player actually burned: A from East Siding west to the Cut, C across the Cut, B from the Cut west through the Long Field to the Pass road. The player sees it first in M9.\n\n**Ending cards:**\n- **Walk out:** *You reached the border with a case of stones and a map nobody else will ever use. The guard asks your trade. You tell him: surveyor.*\n- **Give it to them:** *They crossed at first light, walking on ash. Nobody has asked who lit it. The fever is not finished with you, and you are out of tablets. It is a good view.*\n\n**Attract, tests and dev mode** can jump to any mission start: each mission has a `setup` that puts the world in the right state (`world.reset`, story flags, scars, buddies, loadout), so `dev.startMission('m6')` is one call.\n\n---\n\n## 15. Writing\n\n**Voice.** Weary, literary and exact. Short declarative sentences. Euphemism as cruelty. Gallows humour without a wink. Nobody explains the theme. Nobody is your friend without a price. People are tired, and they're smart. Think of a war correspondent who stopped filing years ago. Don't quote real authors, and don't imitate the source's lines.\n\nEach mission gets 8 to 15 spoken lines in this voice. Each character has a tic: **Vance** invoices (*conclude, regrettable, the matter of*). **Ansa** corrects grammar. **Odile** counts things. **Tibor** talks about returns. **Bakr** tells you what stations used to be called. **Ines** owes people, or they owe her. **Dov** tells a three-sentence story that ends badly. **Mags** narrates what she is doing to you. **Harrow** writes like a surveyor's notebook.\n\nAll game text must be in the HUD font's character set. Subtitle lines stay under 60 characters, two lines at most: split long sentences across lines in sequence.\n\nUse these lines verbatim, and write the rest to match:\n\n- **Bakr, M0:** *Forty miles of track and not one station that remembers its name.* / *They paint the signs over. Whoever won last.* / *You have the look of a man who read about this place. Reading is a good way to visit.* / *Up there they will ask you which side. Say yes.*\n- **Odile:** *Three tablets. The fourth you pay for. I do not mean in stones.* / *I do not need you to be good. I need you to be on time.* / *Sixty-one beds. Forty blankets. You are the math.*\n- **Vance:** *We do not burn villages. We conclude them.* / *The water question has been a great sorrow to this office.* / *Your invoice will be honoured, regrettably.*\n- **Ansa:** *You said less people. Fewer. Fewer people. It will matter by the end of the month.* / *Burn the field. A hungry man learns to read the wind.*\n- **Tibor:** *Everything on this rack has been returned at least once.* / *It fires. If you want it to fire twice, that is a different price.*\n- **Ines:** *I flew for both of them. Neither paid. Get in.* / *You owe me a truck. You owe me several trucks.*\n- **Dov:** *Two fingers I left in this country. I came back to see what they are doing.* / *A man asked me to mine his own road, so he would know where it was safe. He was right for a week.*\n- **Mags:** *Hold still. No, you can't feel that. No, that's normal. Hold still.* / *Not today. Today you owe me money.*\n- **A burning buddy:** *Don't let it be the fire. Please. Not the fire.*\n- **Barks:** *There! In the grass!* / *Who lit that?* / *It's stuck! It's stuck again!* / *Leave him, he's already gone.*\n- **Harrow's margin notes,** one per trig point, in order:\n  1. *A map is a promise made by someone who has already left.*\n  2. *I drew the river where the Company wanted it. The river was slow to comply, but it came round.*\n  3. *Both armies buy from me. The Concord pays on time. The Harvest pays in grain and tears. I have eaten better on the tears.*\n  4. *You will have noticed that you follow roads. I drew those too.*\n  5. *Grass is the only honest border. It goes where the wind tells it, and it keeps a record.*\n  6. *By now you have burned what I marked. Look at it from the ridge. Tell me that is not a line.*\n- **Harrow, M9:** *You are late. I said you would be. Sit down, it won't take long, neither of us has long.* / *I drew the lines that started this. I would like to draw one more.* / *You have been drawing for me. Look at it.* / *Burned grass cannot burn twice. It is the only safe road in the country, and you built it for wages.*\n- **Load-screen epigraphs** (*from Harrow's field notes*): write 12 in the same voice.\n\n---\n\n## 16. UI and UX\n\n**10-foot and controller first.** A PS5 DualSense on a TV at ten feet is the design target. Mouse and keyboard play the same game on the same screens and feel native. Everything is drawn with `ctx.hud` in art pixels; there is no DOM UI at all, so it all works in Node tests. Test the view at 1920×1080.\n\n**Layout rules:**\n- Safe area 24 px horizontal, 14 px vertical.\n- Menu items at scale 2; the smallest text anywhere is scale 1 (subtitles, prompts).\n- At most 6 items on a screen, one idea per screen.\n- No tables, no scroll lists, no web-style data screens. Long content is paged.\n- A focused item has a full-width bar in `orange` and a small marker. Move and confirm sounds.\n- Only the title and pause menus cover the view. Every other screen is in your hands or an overlay with the world visible behind it.\n\n**HUD in play is minimal** and hides 6 s after it last changed:\n- 5 health segments, syrette and tablet counts bottom-left.\n- Ammo and the gun's condition icon bottom-right.\n- A dot reticle (hidden while scoped; the scope has its own black mask).\n- Prompts centre-bottom. Subtitles above them with the speaker's name in a colour.\n- Mission step at the top for 5 s when it changes.\n\n**Controls** (`src/core/actions.js`):\n\n| Action | DualSense | Xbox glyph | Keyboard and mouse |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Move / look | L stick / R stick | same | WASD / mouse |\n| Fire / aim | R2 / L2 | RT / LT | LMB / RMB |\n| Use (when a prompt shows), else reload | Square | X | E / R |\n| Jump | Cross | A | Space |\n| Crouch | Circle | B | C (never Ctrl: Ctrl+W closes the browser tab) |\n| Sprint | L3 (click) | LS | Left Shift |\n| Melee | R3 | RS | F |\n| Next weapon | Triangle | Y | Wheel, or 1-4 |\n| Throw / plant | R1 | RB | G |\n| Syrette, surgery | L1 | LB | Q |\n| Map up / down | D-pad Up | D-pad Up | M or Tab |\n| Tablet | D-pad Down | D-pad Down | H |\n| Tracker | D-pad Left | D-pad Left | T |\n| Monocular (hold) | D-pad Right | D-pad Right | V |\n| Pause | Options | Menu | Esc |\n| Ledger | Create | View | J |\n| **Driving:** gas / brake-reverse / steer | R2 / L2 / L stick | RT / LT / L stick | W / S / A-D |\n| Handbrake | Cross | A | Space |\n| Get out / repair | Square | X | E |\n| Swap to gun | Triangle | Y | F |\n| Chase camera | R3 | RS | C |\n\nUse `input.preventKeys.add('Tab')` etc. Analog triggers: each frame, read `navigator.getGamepads()` buttons 6 and 7 `value` and `input.send({ tr:[l2, r2] })` when changed, so recordings keep it, and use it for throttle and brake. Rumble: `pad.vibrationActuator?.playEffect('dual-rumble', {...})`, guarded, Settings toggle.\n\n**Glyphs.** Prompts follow the input used last:\n- `device` flips to `kbm` on keydown, mouse button or real mouse movement, and to `pad` on any `Pad*` code or a stick past 0.35.\n- `src/ui/glyphs.js` is pixel art as `hud.sprite` rows, about 11 × 11: Cross, Circle, Square, Triangle, L1, L2, R1, R2, L3, R3, D-pad directions, Options, Create; Xbox A, B, X, Y, LB, LT, RB, RT, LS, RS, Menu, View; a key cap drawn around any letter; LMB, RMB, MMB, wheel.\n- Settings has **Glyphs: PlayStation / Xbox**, default PlayStation.\n- `game.state().prompts` lists what's on screen, so tests can check it.\n\n**The mouse is native.** In menus the pointer is free (no lock), hover moves focus, click activates (read `input.buttonEvents`; convert with `x = (p.x+1)/2*hud.width`, `y = (1-p.y)/2*hud.height`). The wheel scrolls pages. Over the world it aims and looks under pointer lock. On the held map it's a cursor (hover focuses a marker, click sets the waypoint). On Tibor's rack and in dialogue choices, click works too. Keyboard in menus: arrows or WASD, Enter or Space, Esc back. Pad in menus: D-pad or left stick with key repeat, Cross confirms, Circle goes back, L1/R1 change tabs and pages. If the pad disconnects during play, open the pause menu.\n\n**The held map** (`src/world/map-texture.js`). The heart of pillar 3.\n- 320 × 240 DataTexture on a plane about 0.5 × 0.375 m, about 0.42 m in front of the camera, tilted, in both hands (the `hand` model and hands rig), filling about 70% of the width, so one texel is about one art pixel. A 0.62 m plane, which I tried first, was too big.\n- Baked at start: contour lines every 8 m on sand paper, river, roads, rail, labels in your own 5×7 `pixfont.js`.\n- Redrawn at up to 2 Hz on a copy: burn scars (ink), your position and heading, the waypoint, sites you've seen, mission step and Harrow's notes in the margin, wind arrow and clock on a small GPS clipped to the corner.\n- Raise and lower takes 0.4 s with paper sound. **The world never stops.** You can walk and drive with it up. While it's up, the look input moves the map cursor.\n- Square/LMB on a marker sets the waypoint; Triangle or wheel toggles a closer zoom.\n- It works at night because the paper uses a dim lit toon plus a small hand torch `lights.request` following the view group.\n\n**Screens:**\n- **Loading:** the engine's, then a black screen with one Harrow epigraph.\n- **Title:** live 3D scene (dusk, fixed slow camera over burning grass on the Long Field, music), the title large (scale 4, or 3 if it won't fit), the latest input's *Press [glyph]*. Then the main menu.\n- **Main menu:** Continue (when a save exists), New Game, Cash Run, Settings, About and Credits.\n- **Pause** (`timeScale = 0`): Resume, Ledger, Settings, Dev Mode, About and Credits, Quit to Title. In a hub session: Resume and Settings only.\n- **Settings:** Sound (Music slider **default 10%**, Effects, Voices), Controls (Look sensitivity for pad, for mouse; Invert Y; Aim assist; Rumble; Glyphs), Picture (Fullscreen, for the TV; Pixel size Fine/Chunky via `engine.settings.set`; Quality; Field of view), Comfort (Subtitle size; Reduce flashes; Fever effects reduced), Reset to Defaults. Saved in your own `localStorage` entry and re-applied at boot: `settings:{ button:false, key:false }` hides the engine's panel and stops the engine saving its own copy.\n- **Dialogue:** the camera holds on the speaker; subtitles; two big buttons at most.\n- **Tibor's rack:** one gun at a time, large (its first-person model turned to the side on a table), name, three bars (Damage, Range, Reliability), price. Left/right cycles. Buy or Take.\n- **Locker:** one row per slot, left/right picks.\n- **Bed:** Dawn, Noon, Dusk, Midnight, Leave.\n- **Ledger:** section 13.\n- **Game Over, Ending card, Credits.**\n- **About and Credits:** paged, see section 27.\n\n**Touch-only devices.** Detect with `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches` and no pad connected (verified: true on Chromium with the `iPhone 14`, `iPad Pro 11` and `Pixel 7` profiles, false on a desktop context). Engine option `touch:false` always, so there are never on-screen controls. On such a device the title shows **Controller or keyboard required** (the exact text in `state().notice`, drawn uppercase by the font) and one large **Settings** button (tap works as click: `input.buttonEvents` reports a finger as code `Touch`). Attract mode still starts after 10 s; a tap exits to this screen. A key press or pad connecting clears the gate and shows the normal title.\n\n---\n\n## 17. Dev mode\n\nPause menu → **Dev Mode** (hidden in a hub session). An overlay with tabs (L1/R1 or Q/E), world visible behind, playing or frozen by a toggle.\n\n| Tab | Contents |\n| --- | --- |\n| Cheats | God mode, infinite ammo, no jams, no fever, invisible to AI, noclip fly |\n| Teleport | Every site, every post, every case, the crosshair point |\n| Spawn | Squad of each faction, pickup, technical, truck, a stone case, a buddy |\n| World | Hour slider, wind direction and speed sliders, weather (clear, dust, storm), ignite at crosshair, extinguish all, regrow all, sleep +6 h |\n| Mission | Start any mission, complete current step, set story flags, give stones, tablets, syrettes, all guns; break gun; force jam; force fever; down a buddy |\n| **Balance** | Live sliders (below), **Reset to Defaults** for all, Square/R resets one |\n| Debug | Fire-grid overlay, nav overlay, AI state text over heads, counts (actors, burning cells, draw info from `engine.state()`), engine debug panel (`engine.showDebug`), free camera (`engine.setCamera({ preset:'free' })`, restored after; re-install `step` in `onCameraChange`), crosshair coordinates for placing things in `src/content/`, Quick Save/Load, show `status()` |\n\n**Balance sliders** (left/right steps, hold accelerates, mouse drags). Defaults in `src/content/tuning-defaults.js`:\n\n| Slider | Default | Range |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `playerSpeed` multiplier | 1 | 0.5-2 |\n| `playerDamageTaken` multiplier | 1 | 0-3 |\n| `weaponDamage` multiplier | 1 | 0.25-4 |\n| `enemyHealth` multiplier | 1 | 0.25-4 |\n| `enemyAccuracy` | 1 | 0.25-3 |\n| `enemyVision` (m) | 90 | 20-200 |\n| `enemyReaction` (s) | 0.45 | 0.1-2 |\n| `wearRate` | 1 | 0-5 |\n| `jamRate` | 1 | 0-5 |\n| `fireSpread` | 1 | 0-3 |\n| `fireDamage` (HP/s) | 8 | 0-30 |\n| `windEffect` | 1 | 0-3 |\n| `feverMinutes` | 12 | 2-40 |\n| `vehicleTopSpeed` (m/s) | 26 | 10-45 |\n| `vehicleToughness` | 1 | 0.25-4 |\n| `stonesReward` multiplier | 1 | 0-5 |\n| `buddyWoundChance` | 0.15 | 0-1 |\n| `dayMinutes` | 30 | 2-120 |\n| `postRemanHours` | 24 | 1-96 |\n| `regrowHours` | 48 | 1-200 |\n\nA test sets every slider, checks the system responds, presses Reset, and checks every value equals its default.\n\n---\n\n## 18. Attract mode\n\nAfter **10 seconds with no input on the title screen or main menu**, start a looping demo (`src/attract/`). Settings and About are exempt, because people stop to read them. It's a director with a list of beats, using the real game with `cam.override`, god mode, infinite ammo and bot input through the same action layer. It cheats freely: teleports, spawns, sets the hour and wind. A `save.disabled` flag stops it touching saves.\n\nBeats (10 to 14 s each, joined by `engine.screen.cover('dither')` and `reveal`), to show as much as possible:\n1. Dusk, driving a technical down the road, first person, raising the map at the wheel.\n2. Rolling into a checkpoint, gunfight, the gun jams, slap and rack.\n3. Flare into dry grass, the wind takes it, soldiers run burning.\n4. Night, the Long Field in flames, chase camera past it.\n5. Fever: the view swims, tablet to mouth.\n6. Field surgery with pliers.\n7. Scoped shot from a ridge at noon.\n8. Dragged out by a buddy; syrette or finish it.\n9. Tracker beeping to a case in a burnt wreck.\n10. Train with the flatcar MG.\n11. Tibor's rack, a line of his.\n12. The map on a table with the scars glowing.\n13. The title.\n\nHUD shows a `DEMO` tag and *Press [glyph]*. **Any input exits** (key, mouse button or real movement, pad button or stick, tap) back to the screen it came from, after `world.reset()`. The loop must run indefinitely without error. It runs behind the touch gate too. Never in a hub session.\n\n---\n\n## 19. Multiplayer\n\nFollow the AI Hub Session Protocol v1 (read `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`; also the shared-world example `examples/arena.html` beside it). The hub runs invites, lobby, names, clock and results; the game runs the round. The same code also plays when the game is on its own.\n\n**Mode: `shared-world`, 1 to 4 players.** Four mercs in one burning valley, friends until the stones are counted.\n\n**The round, \"Cash Run\" (6 minutes):**\n- The valley around the Cut: the campaign's terrain, with only the Cut, P5 and the Ranger Post live, 16 to 24 soldiers, wind and fire on.\n- Six stone cases in guarded spots, shown by the tracker's beep and a marker when close. One extraction truck on the road south of the pit.\n- Everyone starts at a different road end with `tractor` (cond 70), `flare`, `cane`, 2 syrettes, 2 bottles.\n- Carry one case at a time (speed × 0.85, you can't sprint); walk it to the truck to bank its stones. Most stones wins.\n- Down at 0 HP: you drop the case and bleed for 25 s. Another player can hold Use for 3 s to bring you up (+1 Revive) or just take the case. Bleed out and you return at your road end after 15 s. Friendly fire is on: that's the theme.\n- On foot only, in rounds: no player vehicles.\n- Ends when the time is up, or when all cases are banked or burned. Standings by stones, ties together.\n\n**Session head tags** go in the template (section 23): `hub:session` 1, `hub:session-players` `1-4`, `hub:session-mode` `shared-world`, `hub:session-minutes` `6`, `hub:webgpu` `required`, `hub:session-goal` *Carry the most diamond cases out of the burning mine*, `hub:session-howto` *Stick/WASD move, R2/mouse fire, Square/E use, carry cases to the truck*.\n\n**Boot order** (`src/main.js`). This is the part that makes the hub work:\n```js\nconst info = (window.AIHub && AIHub.active) ? await AIHub.connect({ mode:'shared-world', seats:[1,4], card:true }) : null;\nif (info) {\n  const game = createGame({ session: hubSession(info) });        // mode 'round': no title, no menus, no attract\n  if (info.server) { const e = await Engine.headless(game, {}); AIHub.ready(); setInterval(() => e.step(6, 1/60), 100); }\n  else if (!navigator.gpu) AIHub.fail('This game needs WebGPU');\n  else await Engine.start(game, { ...OPTIONS, seed: info.seed });  // game.ready(ctx) calls AIHub.ready() once, with no key press\n} else { /* normal start: touch check, title */ }\n```\nHandle a rejected `__PIXEL_READY__` by `AIHub.fail(message)`. If `connect` answers `null`, run as on your own.\n\n**`src/net/session.js`:** one interface, three implementations, so round code never knows which: `{ kind, me, players:[{id,name,color}], host, isHost, server, time(), rng(label), send(data,{to,reliable}), on(event,fn), ready(), answer(what), finish(outcome), fail(msg) }`.\n- `hubSession` wraps `AIHub`.\n- `soloSession` is **on its own**: host is you, the other seats are AI mercs (reuse the buddy brain: go to the nearest case, bank it, shoot what shoots you), with your own results screen at the end.\n- `linkSession` is **on its own with a friend on the same computer**: `BroadcastChannel('game-link-v1')` between two windows. Host and Join on the Cash Run menu, a simple lobby, `start` carrying a `Date.now()` time base and a seed. It costs little, reuses everything, and is how two-window play gets tested.\n\nThe main menu's Cash Run offers: Solo with Hired Guns, Host on This Computer, Join on This Computer, plus one line saying friends online play through AI Hub.\n\n**Netcode.** The host runs the world. Each copy moves its own player from its own stick, at once, never waiting for the network, as `arena.html` does.\n\n| Message | Direction | Rate, kind | Content |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |","numLines":250,"startLine":600,"totalLines":1129}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SwtLXJFv3h7cu8qS4dqLBX","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgke1pX4F2vwmQprmsyFK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014m8qDEoSfvdg3QBqkG9xc2","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162033__x07393c/work/PLAN.md","offset":850,"limit":300},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10776,"cache_read_input_tokens":53072,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10776},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"feff64bd-df6d-45b2-b337-83604d3a2d73","uuid":"a09fe11e-9aa1-42e8-8d38-5d2dc05316f4","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:20:51.590Z","request_id":"req_011Cgke1pJR4DZK3w3iGRaBF","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_014m8qDEoSfvdg3QBqkG9xc2":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162033__x07393c/work/PLAN.md","offset":850,"limit":300}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014m8qDEoSfvdg3QBqkG9xc2","type":"tool_result","content":"850\t| `me` | client → host | 12/s, unreliable | seq, position, yaw, pitch, stance, weapon, hp echo |\n851\t| `ev` | client → host | up to 5/s, reliable, batched | shots since last batch (origin, dir, weapon), use, pick up, bank, revive, ignite |\n852\t| `s` | host → all | 10/s, unreliable, under 1,100 bytes | time, players, soldiers (`[id,x,z,yaw,state,hp]`, ints, y from terrain), cases |\n853\t| `w` | host → all | up to 4/s, reliable, batched | fire cells ignited and burnt, damage per player, downs, deaths, explosions, banks, sounds |\n854\t\n855\tThat's at most 17 messages a second per copy; the limit is 20 with bursts of 40, and 16 KB per message. **Drive sends from `setInterval`, not the render loop:** on a software-rendered copy `update` runs about twice a second, and traffic must still flow.\n856\t\n857\tClients render soldiers as puppets interpolated 150 ms behind; they run fire visuals only; health is host-authoritative. Local shots show muzzle flash and tracers at once, and the host decides hits. Older snapshots are dropped by `at`. In a shared world use `AIHub.rng(label)`, because `Math.random` isn't seeded there; the world is the same static terrain on all copies anyway.\n858\t\n859\t**The server case.** `AIHub.server` true: run the same host code under `Engine.headless` with no player, camera, audio or HUD (`me` isn't in `players`). Don't touch `info.players[me]`.\n860\t\n861\t**Round rules the harness checks:**\n862\t- `time-up`: the host calls `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, stats, awards })` **directly from the event handler**, within `graceMs` (5 s). Every present player appears once.\n863\t- `leave`: continue; the host finishes if nobody is left.\n864\t- `end`: no more input or sends, `audio.stopMusic()`, `audio.stopLoops()`, mute. The hub shows results.\n865\t- `stats` at most 6 names per player (Stones, Downs, Revives, Kills); `awards` up to 3 (*Last Friend* for most revives, *Paid in Full* for most stones, *Arsonist* for most cells lit).\n866\t\n867\t**In a session:** no title, menus or prompts before the round. No dialogs (`alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`), no `window.open`, no navigation, no network except the hub. Quit does nothing. Names come only from the hub (sanitize to the font's characters; HUD canvas, never HTML). No chat, emotes or custom names. **On a pad, ignore Options while Create is held** (Create + Options is the hub's). Sessions get an empty storage, so settings start at defaults, music at 10%.\n868\t\n869\t**The game's own card** (`card:true`). A shared-world card on your live scene with `GAME_TITLE`, the players in their seat colours with ready marks, how to win, this player's controls in their glyphs, time left from the `card` event. Ready: Enter, Cross, or a tap/click on Ready → `AIHub.answer('ready')`. More time: Triangle, key `M`, or tap → `AIHub.answer('more')`. It has no menus, and play begins only at `start`.\n870\t**Listen for Enter and M with a plain `window` keydown listener** (verified to pass the harness's card check), because the harness expects an answer within 3 s and the render loop may be slow. Pad buttons can poll in `update`. Everything on the card uses `AIHub.rng('card')` for randomness. When `AIHub.time() >= 0` the round is on; show the 3-2-1 countdown before that.\n871\t\n872\t**Fallback.** If shared-world can't be made stable, ship `ghost` (each copy its own world, others' mercs shown, `progress` and `result` by score, `Math.random` seeded for you) rather than drop multiplayer, and last of all `parallel`.\n873\t\n874\t**Test it:** section 24, all four harness scenarios, and two windows on `linkSession`, plus the game outside a session.\n875\t\n876\t---\n877\t\n878\t## 20. Art\n879\t\n880\t**Base style:** the engine's native 3D-as-pixel-art pipeline at 480×270, toon materials, palette colours only. Make new assets for what makes the game feel like its source. The library covers generic props (use it: `crate`, `barrel`, `sack`, `table`, `chair`, `bed`, `stool`, `boulders`, `rock`, `dead-tree`, `bush`, `reeds`, `stone-wall`, `battlement`, `signpost`, `notice-board`, `market-stall`, `well`, `lamp-post`, `campfire`, `rubble`, `mine-rail`, `shovel`). The library has **no guns, vehicles, acacias or modern buildings**: you write those.\n881\t\n882\t**Workflow** (`ASSETS.md`): plain data in `src/art/models.js`; `node check.mjs --sheets src/art/models.js`; open the PNGs; fix; then check in game. Don't re-check what hasn't changed.\n883\t\n884\t**You must make, as `model()` defs:**\n885\t- **People:** soldier (Concord, Harvest; 3 hat variants, 4 `skin` values), mercs (Ines, Dov, Mags, a silhouette each), Odile (veil, cigarette), Tibor (apron), Vance (peaked cap, medals), Ansa (headscarf, spectacles), Harrow (blanket, wide hat), Old Bakr, civilians (4 palettes), all on the rig from section 3.\n886\t- **First-person:** arms and hands (sleeve, skin); `cane`, `m38`, `flare`, `tractor`, `mule`, `empire`, `weed` with tank and hose, `tube`, bottle, charge, detonator; each gun with named rust and tape parts; syrette, tablet bottle, pliers, knife, lighter, wrench, monocular, tracker, map plane, GPS; steering wheel and dash for each vehicle.\n887\t- **Vehicles:** pickup, technical, cargo truck, tanker, burnt wreck palettes of each, locomotive, flatcar, boxcar, handcar as dressing.\n888\t- **Buildings and props:** tin-roof shack, concrete bunker, barracks, watchtower, sandbag run, boom gate, fuel tank, oil drum, silo, water tower, pump station, clinic tent with a green cross, station platform and signal mast, trig pillar, radio mast, mine headframe, sluice house, spoil heap, cage, termite mound, Observatory dome.\n889\t- **Nature:** 3 acacia shapes, bottle tree, scorched versions, thorn bush recolour.\n890\t- **Textures** (as `textureDef`): `grass-flame`, smoke puff if particles aren't enough, rusted metal and tin (or the library's `rust`, `metal-plates`), cracked earth and thatch from the library.\n891\t\n892\t**Colour direction:** sand, orange and red land; plum shadows; slate and white for the Concord; orange and red for the Harvest; green only where water or new growth is, so regrowth reads as an event. Night is navy and ink with fire as the only warm colour.\n893\t\n894\t**Style rules that matter here:** thin parts must be at least 0.06 m and silhouette parts 0.12 m at world scale, but first-person models are held 0.5 m from the eye, so they may be thinner. Set `floats:true`, `collider:'none'` on view models and people. Static scenery merges with `mergeStaticMeshes` where you can.\n895\t\n896\t---\n897\t\n898\t## 21. Animation\n899\t\n900\t**Base:** the engine's native system. `ClipDef` data at 30 fps, `compileClips`, `THREE.AnimationMixer`, `gaitClip` for walks and runs, `Ragdoll`, `SpringChain`, `Squash`, `twoBoneIK`, tweens for small things, `Timeline` for scenes.\n901\t\n902\t**From `HERO_CLIPS`, reused on all people:** Idle, IdleLook, Walk, Run, Crouch, CrouchWalk, Crawl, Sit, SitDown, StandUp, LieIdle, Sleep, Hurt, HitReact, Death, Wave, Shout, Push, Climb. `analyzeClip` and `validateClip` check your own.\n903\t\n904\t**New, on the people rig** (`src/art/clips.js`):\n905\t- **Upper-body, armed versions:** AimIdle, AimWalk (arms holding the rifle, played over the legs), FireRecoil, Reload, ThrowBottle.\n906\t- **New whole-body clips:** BurnPanic (arms flailing, a stumbling run), Beg, Surrender, WoundedSit (clutching a side), DragBackward, CarryOver, DriveSit, UnjamSwear, WalkHandsTied, Shrug (Tibor), SmokeIdle (Odile), CleanRifleIdle (Vance), WriteAtDesk (Harrow), TeachPoint (Ansa).\n907\t\n908\t**To layer upper over lower,** split clips by filtering tracks: `new THREE.AnimationClip(name, clip.duration, clip.tracks.filter(t => /^(Pelvis|Leg|Shin|Foot)/.test(t.name)))`, and the rest for the upper body, then play one of each.\n909\t\n910\t**New, on the hands rig** (`src/art/viewmodels.js` + clips):\n911\t- Idle sway and walk bob (procedural), ADS raise, fire kick per gun.\n912\t- Reload per gun (magazine out and in on `Mag`, bolt on `Bolt`; revolver opens; shells for `mule`; flare breaks open).\n913\t- **Unjam** (slap and rack), **falls apart**, equip and holster.\n914\t- Cane knife swing, throw, plant, detonator click.\n915\t- Tablet to mouth, syrette, **four surgery scenes**, **raise map** and tracker, monocular, wrench on bonnet, hand on wheel and shifter, finish-it.\n916\t\n917\t**Fauna:** gazelle run and graze on its own rig; vulture wing flap.\n918\t\n919\t**Scenes:** use `Timeline` for the M0 ride, the rescue drag, M9, and endings, as `cam.override` plus `lines` and `bars()`. Skip with Cross/Enter (`timeline.skip()`).\n920\t\n921\t---\n922\t\n923\t## 22. Audio\n924\t\n925\tEverything is written in code: `SoundDef` data, `Song` data and generated voices. No audio files. Browsers start sound on the first gesture (the engine handles it; `audio.unlock()` from your own first input). Silent before that, which is fine for attract.\n926\t\n927\t**Music defaults to 10%:** on first boot with no saved settings, `audio.setVolume('music', 0.1)`. The Music slider shows 10%. Your Settings Reset returns it to 0.1 (not `resetVolumes()`, which gives 0.6). Test: clean storage → `audio.volume.music === 0.1`.\n928\t\n929\t**Music** (`Song` data, written for this game, original melodies):\n930\t- At least 6: Title, Day (sparse plucked triangle over a low drone), Night (almost nothing), Stalk (tense pulse), Fire and Fight (hand-drum noise, driving low saw), Fever (a detuned Day), End (one line, unaccompanied).\n931\t- Style: plucked pentatonic lines, thumb-piano timbres (triangle or sine, short decay), noise-based hand drums, low drones; nothing that imitates another game's score.\n932\t- Switch on state with a 12 s minimum dwell, using `audio.playMusic`.\n933\t\n934\t**Effects** (`src/audio/sfx.js`, `audio.register`, layered `SoundDef`s). Every one of these is required:\n935\t- Each gun (noise crack + low thump + a tail, plus a distant muffled variant), jam click, slap, rack, magazine, shell, revolver cylinder, flare pop and hiss, flamethrower roar loop, bottle smash, rocket.\n936\t- Explosion, ricochet, bullet whip, hit flesh, hit metal, gun falling apart.\n937\t- Footsteps by surface (dirt, grass, road, wood, water).\n938\t- Breath, heartbeat, syrette hiss, pliers, knife, finger snap, lighter, tablet bottle, grunt.\n939\t- Fire loop, wind loop, night insects, day birds and cicadas (chirps from arps and vibrato).\n940\t- Engine loop (pitch by speed), gravel, brakes, door, horn, starter cough, wrench, train clack, train whistle.\n941\t- Map paper, tracker beep, radio squelch.\n942\t- Thunder, rain loop, distant gunfire stingers.\n943\t- UI move, confirm, back.\n944\t\n945\tSpatialize with `spatialize` and `voice.set({ muffle })` when blocked. A test renders them all with `renderSound` and checks they aren't silent.\n946\t\n947\t**Voices** (`src/audio/voice.js`): Animalese/Simlish gibberish.\n948\t- For each character: base pitch, syllable rate, wave. A syllable is a short layered `SoundDef`, verified to work: `{ wave:'saw', freq:190, freqEnd:170, attack:.005, decay:.09, volume:.3, layers:[{wave:'sine',freq:760,decay:.08,volume:.18},{wave:'sine',freq:1220,decay:.07,volume:.1},{wave:'noise',freq:6000,decay:.012,volume:.08}] }`.\n949\t- Build about 12 of them (vowel formant pairs × consonant noise).\n950\t- `voice.say(character, text)`: for each word, count vowels, hash the word to pick syllables (so a word always \"sounds\" the same), play at the character's pitch with `pitch` offsets for intonation (rise on `?`, fall on `.`, pause at `,`), at the Voices slider's level.\n951\t- Runs over the subtitle's length; soldiers' barks are spatial.\n952\t\n953\tCheck sound by what Web Audio produces (section 24); nobody can listen here.\n954\t\n955\t---\n956\t\n957\t## 23. Packaging\n958\t\n959\tThe deliverable is **one HTML file** at the place your brief names, beside the dev folder. Nothing else is needed at runtime; no CDN is used. It must run from `file://` and from any web server.\n960\t\n961\t**Head order is strict:**\n962\t```html\n963\t<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head>\n964\t<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n965\t<script>/* vendor/session.js pasted unmodified, as the first script */</script>\n966\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\"> ... the tags from section 19 ...\n967\t<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n968\t<title>GAME_TITLE</title>\n969\t</head><body><div id=\"app\"></div><script type=\"module\">/* the bundle */</script></body></html>\n970\t```\n971\t\n972\t`tools/build.mjs` (the steps I ran, with `</script` escaped; set `OUT` from your brief):\n973\t```js\n974\tconst js = execFileSync('esbuild', ['src/main.js','--bundle','--format=esm','--target=esnext','--legal-comments=inline','--log-level=warning'], { maxBuffer: 1 << 29 }).toString();\n975\tconst session = readFileSync('vendor/session.js','utf8');\n976\tconst html = TEMPLATE.replace('%SESSION%', () => session.replace(/<\\/script/gi,'<\\\\/script')).replace('%BUNDLE%', () => js.replace(/<\\/script/gi,'<\\\\/script'));\n977\twriteFileSync(OUT, html);\n978\t```\n979\tUse function replacers as above, because the engine contains `$` sequences. The bundle is about 5.3 MB before your game is added. Append the licence texts of the engine, three.js and Rapier from the kit's `CREDITS.md` as an HTML comment at the end of the file. esbuild bundles `pixel-engine.js` without you editing it; that satisfies \"keep the engine as it ships\".\n980\t\n981\t`src/main.js` is the only module that starts the engine. Start options:\n982\t```js\n983\tconst OPTIONS = withUrlOptions({ container: document.getElementById('app'), camera:{ preset:'first', fov:62 }, look: LOOK, touch:false, debugKeys:false, settings:{ button:false, key:false } });\n984\t```\n985\t`withUrlOptions` keeps the review flags (`?seed=`, `?debug=1`, `?look=`), which are useful and harmless. `debugKeys:false` keeps the engine's R, P and M hotkeys from colliding with yours; dev mode has its own tools.\n986\t\n987\t---\n988\t\n989\t## 24. Testing\n990\t\n991\tTest as much as you like with headless tools. **One command:** `node tests/run.mjs`. It prints only failures and a one-line count, like `412 passed, 0 failed, 3 suites unchanged`. To rerun only after changing covered code, it hashes each suite's covered files into `tests/.stamps.json` and skips unchanged suites unless given `--all`. `--only <suite>` runs one. **Don't use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.** Log what testing catches in `tests/ISSUES.md`.\n992\t\n993\t**Suites:**\n994\t\n995\t1. **`static` (Node):** in `src/`: no `Math.random`; no `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder`, `stub`, `coming soon`. Every string in `src/content/` uses only the font's characters; every model passes `checkModel`, every texture `validateTexture`; every `Song` parses; every sound renders non-silent; every mission's site, tag, line and buddy resolves; every `TUNING` key has a slider or a reason.\n996\t\n997\t2. **`systems` (Node, `Engine.headless`, driven by `e.step` and actions):**\n998\t   - fire head speed 2-5 m/s, can't cross a road without strong wind, burnt can't re-burn, regrowth, save round-trip of the grid\n999\t   - wear math and jam frequency against the formula; jam blocks fire; reload clears it; gun falls apart at 0\n1000\t   - hit zones; syrette; surgery; down-with-buddy, down-without\n1001\t   - fever: tablet clears it, ignoring collapses and costs stones\n1002\t   - perception by stance and night; pass exemption; soldier burn panic\n1003\t   - vehicle drive to waypoint, damage thresholds, repair, explode\n1004\t   - map up while driving; cursor sets the waypoint\n1005\t   - tracker rate; trig note; post cleared then re-manned; rail halt; shop purchase; locker; sleep to hour; save and load\n1006\t   - pause (`timeScale` 0), menus by pad, by keyboard, by mouse hover and click\n1007\t   - device switch changes `prompts` glyphs; Xbox setting; settings persistence; music 0.1\n1008\t   - sliders and Reset; attract starts at frame 601 with no input, not before; any input exits; saves untouched; touch gate state with `matchMedia` stubbed\n1009\t   - round rules (solo session): bank, drop, revive, time-up finish\n1010\t\n1011\t3. **`playthrough` (Node):** a bot plays M0 through both endings, using `dev.teleport` between objectives but real actions for every objective (drive the truck, burn the tanks, plant the charge, choose at the buddy). It runs with god mode on and with buddies alive, and once with one buddy dead. After each mission, assert the world state and Ledger. This is the most important test.\n1012\t\n1013\t4. **`replay` (Node):** record one mission segment, replay it, compare `engine.fingerprint()`.\n1014\t\n1015\t5. **`browser` (Playwright, one Chromium):** the built single file on `file://`, 1920×1080, with these flags (the ones `check.mjs` uses; correct frames came from them):\n1016\t   `['--enable-unsafe-webgpu','--enable-features=Vulkan','--use-vulkan=swiftshader','--use-angle=swiftshader','--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader']`.\n1017\t   Check:\n1018\t   - no page, console, game or GPU errors; backend WebGPU\n1019\t   - `AIHub.active` false\n1020\t   - title reached; mouse hover moves focus; click activates\n1021\t   - pad stub via `addInitScript` (`navigator.getGamepads = () => [pad]`); keyboard flows\n1022\t   - sound by `OfflineAudioContext` rendering of `renderSound` output, or an `AnalyserNode` on `audio.context` after a gesture\n1023\t   - a phone profile in Chromium (Playwright's `iPhone 14` device, dropping its default browser type, then tap with `page.touchscreen`): shows the notice and Settings, tap opens Settings, attract runs\n1024\t\n1025\t6. **`hub` (Playwright + a server you started):** copy the built file to `tests/.site/game.html` beside a copy of `vendor/hub/*` (the harness only loads same-origin pages), serve that folder on `127.0.0.1` with an OS-picked port (`python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, read the port, kill it by its PID at the end), confirm the page's `<title>`, then for each scenario open `harness.html?game=game.html&<scenario>` and wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, passing when `window.__hubCheck.pass` is true:\n1026\t   - `players=2&auto=1`\n1027\t   - `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`\n1028\t   - `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave`\n1029\t   - `players=2&auto=1&scenario=server`\n1030\t   Run them one at a time. They take about 15 s each here. Print `__hubCheck.checks` entries that failed.\n1031\t\n1032\t7. **`link` (Playwright, two pages of one context on `file://`):** two windows on `linkSession` play a round to its end, with a shared fire, a shared case, and same standings.\n1033\t\n1034\t**Screenshots** only for what a script can't check, at 1920×1080, once each near the end, and whenever you've changed the art they show: title; day first-person with gun; night fire; held map in a truck; Tibor's rack; dialogue; surgery; dev sliders; hub card; ending. Set `e.manual = false`, wait until 10 s or more have passed, and take the screenshot; about 1 frame a second is normal here.\n1035\t\n1036\t**Stand-ins for what this computer lacks** (your brief; runs have no display, so everything here is headless): a pad stub, Playwright phone profiles, Web Audio measurement, two pages for a second player, WebKit iPhone only as a rough touch-layout check (the engine needs WebGPU, so expect its failure message and test the notice logic with Chromium's phone profile), and 1920×1080 screenshots for the TV view.\n1037\t\n1038\t---\n1039\t\n1040\t## 25. Build order\n1041\t\n1042\tEach step ends with a playable build and passing tests, and leaves nothing half-done. Do them in order. Write sound, feedback and tests with each feature rather than at the end.\n1043\t\n1044\t| Step | Do | Done when |\n1045\t| --- | --- | --- |\n1046\t| 0 Pipeline | Pick the title. Unzip the kit. Download `vendor/`. `tools/build.mjs`, `tests/run.mjs` with the hub suite. A blank `createGame()` with a shared-world round that does nothing | Single file opens on `file://`; **all four hub scenarios pass from day one**. Keep them passing |\n1047\t| 1 Walk | Terrain, roads, river, sky, wind, grass, trees. Player, `installLook`, actions, pad codes, device tracking, HUD basics, pause | You can walk the Kettle by pad or mouse |\n1048\t| 2 Shoot | Hands rig and `tractor` first, soldier rig, one AI squad, damage, health, syrette, wear, jam, reload. SFX for each | A fight at P2 is fun on its own. Add the other guns |\n1049\t| 3 Burn | Fire grid, flare, bottle, flamethrower, scars, regrowth, soldier panic, day and night. Fire sounds | Lighting a field at night makes you stop and watch |\n1050\t| 4 Drive | Vehicles, driving view, damage, repair, patrols, posts, train | Run a checkpoint in a pickup and break down after |\n1051\t| 5 World | All sites, safehouses, Tibor, stones, tracker, fever, tablets, surgery, monocular, held map, rail halts, trig points, save and load | A whole session without missions works |\n1052\t| 6 Story | Mission runner, dialogue, voices, buddies, rescues, M0 to End, Ledger, endings. Playthrough suite | A bot and you both finish it |\n1053\t| 7 Shell | Title, all menus, settings, glyph sets, About, touch gate, attract, dev mode | Every screen works by pad, keyboard and mouse |\n1054\t| 8 Multiplayer | Sim/view puppets, host, client, sessions, Cash Run, card, solo bots, link | Hub and link suites pass with a real round |\n1055\t| 9 Polish | All music, ambience, feel, art passes, balance with the sliders, screenshots | You'd show it to someone |\n1056\t| 10 Ship | Final build, About pages, exit interview, chat reply, `node tests/run.mjs --all` | Section 27 is all true |\n1057\t\n1058\t---\n1059\t\n1060\t## 26. Cut order\n1061\t\n1062\tIf you can't finish everything, cut whole things from the top of this list. Don't leave stubs, and remove all traces (menu entries, map marks, lines). Keep every feature in the demo reachable and shown.\n1063\t\n1064\t1. Fauna (vultures first).\n1065\t2. Same-computer link (keep hub and solo).\n1066\t3. The game's own hub card (use the hub's card: `card:false`).\n1067\t4. Chase camera; dust weather.\n1068\t5. Mercy Runs after the first; trig points down to 3; cases down to 6.\n1069\t6. M5 (Mags offers her alternate plan in M6 instead: get the field workers out first, for less pay).\n1070\t7. M4 (give the tracker in M3; use the MG in M7; Dov joins at the bar).\n1071\t8. M8 (the column just starts walking after M7).\n1072\t9. Shared-world → ghost → parallel (section 19).\n1073\t\n1074\tNever cut: fire, wear and jams, fever, the held map, buddy rescue and the finish-it choice, Harrow's twist, dev mode with sliders, attract mode, glyphs and native mouse, touch gate, the hub check, music at 10%, the voices.\n1075\t\n1076\t---\n1077\t\n1078\t## 27. Done, reports, coverage\n1079\t\n1080\t**Done means:** every line below is true and you've checked it.\n1081\t- [ ] Your title, chosen by the brief's procedure, appears on the title screen and in `<title>`.\n1082\t- [ ] The one HTML file runs from `file://` with nothing else beside it.\n1083\t- [ ] `node tests/run.mjs --all` reports 0 failed.\n1084\t- [ ] All four hub scenarios pass, and the game still runs outside a session.\n1085\t- [ ] You finished the game yourself by bot, both endings.\n1086\t- [ ] No TODOs, placeholders or stubbed features anywhere.\n1087\t- [ ] Every screen shows native prompts for pad (PlayStation and Xbox glyphs) and keyboard/mouse.\n1088\t- [ ] You looked at the screenshots.\n1089\t- [ ] `pixel-engine.js` is byte-identical to the copy in the kit's zip (keep the zip in `vendor/` and compare in the `static` suite).\n1090\t\n1091\t**About and Credits screen** (in-game, paged, reached from main menu and pause; text in `src/content/about.js`). Your brief marks this as critical. It must show:\n1092\t- **Source Information,** with every field your brief lists: Date (from your brief), Source (Far Cry 2), Plan (the file name of this plan as you received it), Genre and Perspective, Tech (engine and its version, three.js r186, Rapier 0.20, esbuild, your additions), Art Direction, Animation, Audio, Online, Testing, Research, Environment, Model (from your brief), and Usage: *added on import*. Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\n1093\t- **Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback:** your brief's questions and your honest answers, in order, each on its own page. Don't estimate cost.\n1094\t- **Credits:** Pixel Engine (MIT), three.js (MIT), Rapier (Apache-2.0), the AI Hub session client, and \"Inspired by Far Cry 2; not affiliated\".\n1095\t\n1096\t**Your final chat reply** repeats the same Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback.\n1097\t\n1098\t**The exit interview file** your brief specifies goes beside the HTML, in the exact JSON shape it gives, every value filled, and must parse. Suggested catalogue values: type `Game`; genre `Shooter`; source `Far Cry 2`; series `Far Cry`; players `1–4`; tags such as `first-person`, `pixel art`, `co-op`, `versus`, `vehicles`, `story`; the name is your title.\n1099\t\n1100\t**Where each line of your brief is covered:**\n1101\t\n1102\t| Brief item | Section |\n1103\t| --- | --- |\n1104\t| Source, original game, capture world, characters, themes, tone | 1, 2, 15 |\n1105\t| Genre, perspective | 1 |\n1106\t| Title by random pick (left to you) | top, 25 |\n1107\t| Research | 3 (done for you; research more if you want) |\n1108\t| Single HTML package, CDN allowance, bundle into root | 23 |\n1109\t| Engine kit kept as shipped, systems added on top | 3, 4, 23 |\n1110\t| Art direction: native base, new assets, library for generic props | 20 |\n1111\t| Animation: native base, new animations | 21 |\n1112\t| Audio in code, Animalese voices, music 10% | 22 |\n1113\t| Online and multiplayer, in the hub and on its own | 19 |\n1114\t| Dev subfolder, what not to read, shared ports and processes | 4, 24 |\n1115\t| Performance out of scope | 3 |\n1116\t| Testing: headless, scripted playthrough, one command, screenshots only when needed, no review subagents | 24 |\n1117\t| Effort | Yours to spend; 25 and 26 order it |\n1118\t| This computer and its stand-ins | 3, 4, 24 |\n1119\t| Feature-complete vertical slice, infrastructure for later build-out | 4, 14, 25 |\n1120\t| Dev mode from pause, standard tools, live sliders, reset | 17 |\n1121\t| Attract mode at 10 s, any input exits | 18 |\n1122\t| Narrative tone | 15 |\n1123\t| 10-foot controller first, native keyboard and mouse, hover focus, glyphs, Xbox option | 16 |\n1124\t| No dense web-style screens | 16 |\n1125\t| Touch-only notice, settings button, attract runs | 16, 18 |\n1126\t| Done: no TODOs, placeholders or stubs | top, 26, 27 |\n1127\t| Source Information, feedback sections, chat reply, About screen | 27 |\n1128\t| Exit interview | 27 |\n1129\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"feff64bd-df6d-45b2-b337-83604d3a2d73","uuid":"9ed7c9a6-8725-41bf-8421-dfa4c86bc3ca","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:20:51.751Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162033__x07393c/work/PLAN.md","content":"| `me` | client → host | 12/s, unreliable | seq, position, yaw, pitch, stance, weapon, hp echo |\n| `ev` | client → host | up to 5/s, reliable, batched | shots since last batch (origin, dir, weapon), use, pick up, bank, revive, ignite |\n| `s` | host → all | 10/s, unreliable, under 1,100 bytes | time, players, soldiers (`[id,x,z,yaw,state,hp]`, ints, y from terrain), cases |\n| `w` | host → all | up to 4/s, reliable, batched | fire cells ignited and burnt, damage per player, downs, deaths, explosions, banks, sounds |\n\nThat's at most 17 messages a second per copy; the limit is 20 with bursts of 40, and 16 KB per message. **Drive sends from `setInterval`, not the render loop:** on a software-rendered copy `update` runs about twice a second, and traffic must still flow.\n\nClients render soldiers as puppets interpolated 150 ms behind; they run fire visuals only; health is host-authoritative. Local shots show muzzle flash and tracers at once, and the host decides hits. Older snapshots are dropped by `at`. In a shared world use `AIHub.rng(label)`, because `Math.random` isn't seeded there; the world is the same static terrain on all copies anyway.\n\n**The server case.** `AIHub.server` true: run the same host code under `Engine.headless` with no player, camera, audio or HUD (`me` isn't in `players`). Don't touch `info.players[me]`.\n\n**Round rules the harness checks:**\n- `time-up`: the host calls `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, stats, awards })` **directly from the event handler**, within `graceMs` (5 s). Every present player appears once.\n- `leave`: continue; the host finishes if nobody is left.\n- `end`: no more input or sends, `audio.stopMusic()`, `audio.stopLoops()`, mute. The hub shows results.\n- `stats` at most 6 names per player (Stones, Downs, Revives, Kills); `awards` up to 3 (*Last Friend* for most revives, *Paid in Full* for most stones, *Arsonist* for most cells lit).\n\n**In a session:** no title, menus or prompts before the round. No dialogs (`alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`), no `window.open`, no navigation, no network except the hub. Quit does nothing. Names come only from the hub (sanitize to the font's characters; HUD canvas, never HTML). No chat, emotes or custom names. **On a pad, ignore Options while Create is held** (Create + Options is the hub's). Sessions get an empty storage, so settings start at defaults, music at 10%.\n\n**The game's own card** (`card:true`). A shared-world card on your live scene with `GAME_TITLE`, the players in their seat colours with ready marks, how to win, this player's controls in their glyphs, time left from the `card` event. Ready: Enter, Cross, or a tap/click on Ready → `AIHub.answer('ready')`. More time: Triangle, key `M`, or tap → `AIHub.answer('more')`. It has no menus, and play begins only at `start`.\n**Listen for Enter and M with a plain `window` keydown listener** (verified to pass the harness's card check), because the harness expects an answer within 3 s and the render loop may be slow. Pad buttons can poll in `update`. Everything on the card uses `AIHub.rng('card')` for randomness. When `AIHub.time() >= 0` the round is on; show the 3-2-1 countdown before that.\n\n**Fallback.** If shared-world can't be made stable, ship `ghost` (each copy its own world, others' mercs shown, `progress` and `result` by score, `Math.random` seeded for you) rather than drop multiplayer, and last of all `parallel`.\n\n**Test it:** section 24, all four harness scenarios, and two windows on `linkSession`, plus the game outside a session.\n\n---\n\n## 20. Art\n\n**Base style:** the engine's native 3D-as-pixel-art pipeline at 480×270, toon materials, palette colours only. Make new assets for what makes the game feel like its source. The library covers generic props (use it: `crate`, `barrel`, `sack`, `table`, `chair`, `bed`, `stool`, `boulders`, `rock`, `dead-tree`, `bush`, `reeds`, `stone-wall`, `battlement`, `signpost`, `notice-board`, `market-stall`, `well`, `lamp-post`, `campfire`, `rubble`, `mine-rail`, `shovel`). The library has **no guns, vehicles, acacias or modern buildings**: you write those.\n\n**Workflow** (`ASSETS.md`): plain data in `src/art/models.js`; `node check.mjs --sheets src/art/models.js`; open the PNGs; fix; then check in game. Don't re-check what hasn't changed.\n\n**You must make, as `model()` defs:**\n- **People:** soldier (Concord, Harvest; 3 hat variants, 4 `skin` values), mercs (Ines, Dov, Mags, a silhouette each), Odile (veil, cigarette), Tibor (apron), Vance (peaked cap, medals), Ansa (headscarf, spectacles), Harrow (blanket, wide hat), Old Bakr, civilians (4 palettes), all on the rig from section 3.\n- **First-person:** arms and hands (sleeve, skin); `cane`, `m38`, `flare`, `tractor`, `mule`, `empire`, `weed` with tank and hose, `tube`, bottle, charge, detonator; each gun with named rust and tape parts; syrette, tablet bottle, pliers, knife, lighter, wrench, monocular, tracker, map plane, GPS; steering wheel and dash for each vehicle.\n- **Vehicles:** pickup, technical, cargo truck, tanker, burnt wreck palettes of each, locomotive, flatcar, boxcar, handcar as dressing.\n- **Buildings and props:** tin-roof shack, concrete bunker, barracks, watchtower, sandbag run, boom gate, fuel tank, oil drum, silo, water tower, pump station, clinic tent with a green cross, station platform and signal mast, trig pillar, radio mast, mine headframe, sluice house, spoil heap, cage, termite mound, Observatory dome.\n- **Nature:** 3 acacia shapes, bottle tree, scorched versions, thorn bush recolour.\n- **Textures** (as `textureDef`): `grass-flame`, smoke puff if particles aren't enough, rusted metal and tin (or the library's `rust`, `metal-plates`), cracked earth and thatch from the library.\n\n**Colour direction:** sand, orange and red land; plum shadows; slate and white for the Concord; orange and red for the Harvest; green only where water or new growth is, so regrowth reads as an event. Night is navy and ink with fire as the only warm colour.\n\n**Style rules that matter here:** thin parts must be at least 0.06 m and silhouette parts 0.12 m at world scale, but first-person models are held 0.5 m from the eye, so they may be thinner. Set `floats:true`, `collider:'none'` on view models and people. Static scenery merges with `mergeStaticMeshes` where you can.\n\n---\n\n## 21. Animation\n\n**Base:** the engine's native system. `ClipDef` data at 30 fps, `compileClips`, `THREE.AnimationMixer`, `gaitClip` for walks and runs, `Ragdoll`, `SpringChain`, `Squash`, `twoBoneIK`, tweens for small things, `Timeline` for scenes.\n\n**From `HERO_CLIPS`, reused on all people:** Idle, IdleLook, Walk, Run, Crouch, CrouchWalk, Crawl, Sit, SitDown, StandUp, LieIdle, Sleep, Hurt, HitReact, Death, Wave, Shout, Push, Climb. `analyzeClip` and `validateClip` check your own.\n\n**New, on the people rig** (`src/art/clips.js`):\n- **Upper-body, armed versions:** AimIdle, AimWalk (arms holding the rifle, played over the legs), FireRecoil, Reload, ThrowBottle.\n- **New whole-body clips:** BurnPanic (arms flailing, a stumbling run), Beg, Surrender, WoundedSit (clutching a side), DragBackward, CarryOver, DriveSit, UnjamSwear, WalkHandsTied, Shrug (Tibor), SmokeIdle (Odile), CleanRifleIdle (Vance), WriteAtDesk (Harrow), TeachPoint (Ansa).\n\n**To layer upper over lower,** split clips by filtering tracks: `new THREE.AnimationClip(name, clip.duration, clip.tracks.filter(t => /^(Pelvis|Leg|Shin|Foot)/.test(t.name)))`, and the rest for the upper body, then play one of each.\n\n**New, on the hands rig** (`src/art/viewmodels.js` + clips):\n- Idle sway and walk bob (procedural), ADS raise, fire kick per gun.\n- Reload per gun (magazine out and in on `Mag`, bolt on `Bolt`; revolver opens; shells for `mule`; flare breaks open).\n- **Unjam** (slap and rack), **falls apart**, equip and holster.\n- Cane knife swing, throw, plant, detonator click.\n- Tablet to mouth, syrette, **four surgery scenes**, **raise map** and tracker, monocular, wrench on bonnet, hand on wheel and shifter, finish-it.\n\n**Fauna:** gazelle run and graze on its own rig; vulture wing flap.\n\n**Scenes:** use `Timeline` for the M0 ride, the rescue drag, M9, and endings, as `cam.override` plus `lines` and `bars()`. Skip with Cross/Enter (`timeline.skip()`).\n\n---\n\n## 22. Audio\n\nEverything is written in code: `SoundDef` data, `Song` data and generated voices. No audio files. Browsers start sound on the first gesture (the engine handles it; `audio.unlock()` from your own first input). Silent before that, which is fine for attract.\n\n**Music defaults to 10%:** on first boot with no saved settings, `audio.setVolume('music', 0.1)`. The Music slider shows 10%. Your Settings Reset returns it to 0.1 (not `resetVolumes()`, which gives 0.6). Test: clean storage → `audio.volume.music === 0.1`.\n\n**Music** (`Song` data, written for this game, original melodies):\n- At least 6: Title, Day (sparse plucked triangle over a low drone), Night (almost nothing), Stalk (tense pulse), Fire and Fight (hand-drum noise, driving low saw), Fever (a detuned Day), End (one line, unaccompanied).\n- Style: plucked pentatonic lines, thumb-piano timbres (triangle or sine, short decay), noise-based hand drums, low drones; nothing that imitates another game's score.\n- Switch on state with a 12 s minimum dwell, using `audio.playMusic`.\n\n**Effects** (`src/audio/sfx.js`, `audio.register`, layered `SoundDef`s). Every one of these is required:\n- Each gun (noise crack + low thump + a tail, plus a distant muffled variant), jam click, slap, rack, magazine, shell, revolver cylinder, flare pop and hiss, flamethrower roar loop, bottle smash, rocket.\n- Explosion, ricochet, bullet whip, hit flesh, hit metal, gun falling apart.\n- Footsteps by surface (dirt, grass, road, wood, water).\n- Breath, heartbeat, syrette hiss, pliers, knife, finger snap, lighter, tablet bottle, grunt.\n- Fire loop, wind loop, night insects, day birds and cicadas (chirps from arps and vibrato).\n- Engine loop (pitch by speed), gravel, brakes, door, horn, starter cough, wrench, train clack, train whistle.\n- Map paper, tracker beep, radio squelch.\n- Thunder, rain loop, distant gunfire stingers.\n- UI move, confirm, back.\n\nSpatialize with `spatialize` and `voice.set({ muffle })` when blocked. A test renders them all with `renderSound` and checks they aren't silent.\n\n**Voices** (`src/audio/voice.js`): Animalese/Simlish gibberish.\n- For each character: base pitch, syllable rate, wave. A syllable is a short layered `SoundDef`, verified to work: `{ wave:'saw', freq:190, freqEnd:170, attack:.005, decay:.09, volume:.3, layers:[{wave:'sine',freq:760,decay:.08,volume:.18},{wave:'sine',freq:1220,decay:.07,volume:.1},{wave:'noise',freq:6000,decay:.012,volume:.08}] }`.\n- Build about 12 of them (vowel formant pairs × consonant noise).\n- `voice.say(character, text)`: for each word, count vowels, hash the word to pick syllables (so a word always \"sounds\" the same), play at the character's pitch with `pitch` offsets for intonation (rise on `?`, fall on `.`, pause at `,`), at the Voices slider's level.\n- Runs over the subtitle's length; soldiers' barks are spatial.\n\nCheck sound by what Web Audio produces (section 24); nobody can listen here.\n\n---\n\n## 23. Packaging\n\nThe deliverable is **one HTML file** at the place your brief names, beside the dev folder. Nothing else is needed at runtime; no CDN is used. It must run from `file://` and from any web server.\n\n**Head order is strict:**\n```html\n<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<script>/* vendor/session.js pasted unmodified, as the first script */</script>\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\"> ... the tags from section 19 ...\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>GAME_TITLE</title>\n</head><body><div id=\"app\"></div><script type=\"module\">/* the bundle */</script></body></html>\n```\n\n`tools/build.mjs` (the steps I ran, with `</script` escaped; set `OUT` from your brief):\n```js\nconst js = execFileSync('esbuild', ['src/main.js','--bundle','--format=esm','--target=esnext','--legal-comments=inline','--log-level=warning'], { maxBuffer: 1 << 29 }).toString();\nconst session = readFileSync('vendor/session.js','utf8');\nconst html = TEMPLATE.replace('%SESSION%', () => session.replace(/<\\/script/gi,'<\\\\/script')).replace('%BUNDLE%', () => js.replace(/<\\/script/gi,'<\\\\/script'));\nwriteFileSync(OUT, html);\n```\nUse function replacers as above, because the engine contains `$` sequences. The bundle is about 5.3 MB before your game is added. Append the licence texts of the engine, three.js and Rapier from the kit's `CREDITS.md` as an HTML comment at the end of the file. esbuild bundles `pixel-engine.js` without you editing it; that satisfies \"keep the engine as it ships\".\n\n`src/main.js` is the only module that starts the engine. Start options:\n```js\nconst OPTIONS = withUrlOptions({ container: document.getElementById('app'), camera:{ preset:'first', fov:62 }, look: LOOK, touch:false, debugKeys:false, settings:{ button:false, key:false } });\n```\n`withUrlOptions` keeps the review flags (`?seed=`, `?debug=1`, `?look=`), which are useful and harmless. `debugKeys:false` keeps the engine's R, P and M hotkeys from colliding with yours; dev mode has its own tools.\n\n---\n\n## 24. Testing\n\nTest as much as you like with headless tools. **One command:** `node tests/run.mjs`. It prints only failures and a one-line count, like `412 passed, 0 failed, 3 suites unchanged`. To rerun only after changing covered code, it hashes each suite's covered files into `tests/.stamps.json` and skips unchanged suites unless given `--all`. `--only <suite>` runs one. **Don't use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.** Log what testing catches in `tests/ISSUES.md`.\n\n**Suites:**\n\n1. **`static` (Node):** in `src/`: no `Math.random`; no `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder`, `stub`, `coming soon`. Every string in `src/content/` uses only the font's characters; every model passes `checkModel`, every texture `validateTexture`; every `Song` parses; every sound renders non-silent; every mission's site, tag, line and buddy resolves; every `TUNING` key has a slider or a reason.\n\n2. **`systems` (Node, `Engine.headless`, driven by `e.step` and actions):**\n   - fire head speed 2-5 m/s, can't cross a road without strong wind, burnt can't re-burn, regrowth, save round-trip of the grid\n   - wear math and jam frequency against the formula; jam blocks fire; reload clears it; gun falls apart at 0\n   - hit zones; syrette; surgery; down-with-buddy, down-without\n   - fever: tablet clears it, ignoring collapses and costs stones\n   - perception by stance and night; pass exemption; soldier burn panic\n   - vehicle drive to waypoint, damage thresholds, repair, explode\n   - map up while driving; cursor sets the waypoint\n   - tracker rate; trig note; post cleared then re-manned; rail halt; shop purchase; locker; sleep to hour; save and load\n   - pause (`timeScale` 0), menus by pad, by keyboard, by mouse hover and click\n   - device switch changes `prompts` glyphs; Xbox setting; settings persistence; music 0.1\n   - sliders and Reset; attract starts at frame 601 with no input, not before; any input exits; saves untouched; touch gate state with `matchMedia` stubbed\n   - round rules (solo session): bank, drop, revive, time-up finish\n\n3. **`playthrough` (Node):** a bot plays M0 through both endings, using `dev.teleport` between objectives but real actions for every objective (drive the truck, burn the tanks, plant the charge, choose at the buddy). It runs with god mode on and with buddies alive, and once with one buddy dead. After each mission, assert the world state and Ledger. This is the most important test.\n\n4. **`replay` (Node):** record one mission segment, replay it, compare `engine.fingerprint()`.\n\n5. **`browser` (Playwright, one Chromium):** the built single file on `file://`, 1920×1080, with these flags (the ones `check.mjs` uses; correct frames came from them):\n   `['--enable-unsafe-webgpu','--enable-features=Vulkan','--use-vulkan=swiftshader','--use-angle=swiftshader','--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader']`.\n   Check:\n   - no page, console, game or GPU errors; backend WebGPU\n   - `AIHub.active` false\n   - title reached; mouse hover moves focus; click activates\n   - pad stub via `addInitScript` (`navigator.getGamepads = () => [pad]`); keyboard flows\n   - sound by `OfflineAudioContext` rendering of `renderSound` output, or an `AnalyserNode` on `audio.context` after a gesture\n   - a phone profile in Chromium (Playwright's `iPhone 14` device, dropping its default browser type, then tap with `page.touchscreen`): shows the notice and Settings, tap opens Settings, attract runs\n\n6. **`hub` (Playwright + a server you started):** copy the built file to `tests/.site/game.html` beside a copy of `vendor/hub/*` (the harness only loads same-origin pages), serve that folder on `127.0.0.1` with an OS-picked port (`python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, read the port, kill it by its PID at the end), confirm the page's `<title>`, then for each scenario open `harness.html?game=game.html&<scenario>` and wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, passing when `window.__hubCheck.pass` is true:\n   - `players=2&auto=1`\n   - `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`\n   - `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave`\n   - `players=2&auto=1&scenario=server`\n   Run them one at a time. They take about 15 s each here. Print `__hubCheck.checks` entries that failed.\n\n7. **`link` (Playwright, two pages of one context on `file://`):** two windows on `linkSession` play a round to its end, with a shared fire, a shared case, and same standings.\n\n**Screenshots** only for what a script can't check, at 1920×1080, once each near the end, and whenever you've changed the art they show: title; day first-person with gun; night fire; held map in a truck; Tibor's rack; dialogue; surgery; dev sliders; hub card; ending. Set `e.manual = false`, wait until 10 s or more have passed, and take the screenshot; about 1 frame a second is normal here.\n\n**Stand-ins for what this computer lacks** (your brief; runs have no display, so everything here is headless): a pad stub, Playwright phone profiles, Web Audio measurement, two pages for a second player, WebKit iPhone only as a rough touch-layout check (the engine needs WebGPU, so expect its failure message and test the notice logic with Chromium's phone profile), and 1920×1080 screenshots for the TV view.\n\n---\n\n## 25. Build order\n\nEach step ends with a playable build and passing tests, and leaves nothing half-done. Do them in order. Write sound, feedback and tests with each feature rather than at the end.\n\n| Step | Do | Done when |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 0 Pipeline | Pick the title. Unzip the kit. Download `vendor/`. `tools/build.mjs`, `tests/run.mjs` with the hub suite. A blank `createGame()` with a shared-world round that does nothing | Single file opens on `file://`; **all four hub scenarios pass from day one**. Keep them passing |\n| 1 Walk | Terrain, roads, river, sky, wind, grass, trees. Player, `installLook`, actions, pad codes, device tracking, HUD basics, pause | You can walk the Kettle by pad or mouse |\n| 2 Shoot | Hands rig and `tractor` first, soldier rig, one AI squad, damage, health, syrette, wear, jam, reload. SFX for each | A fight at P2 is fun on its own. Add the other guns |\n| 3 Burn | Fire grid, flare, bottle, flamethrower, scars, regrowth, soldier panic, day and night. Fire sounds | Lighting a field at night makes you stop and watch |\n| 4 Drive | Vehicles, driving view, damage, repair, patrols, posts, train | Run a checkpoint in a pickup and break down after |\n| 5 World | All sites, safehouses, Tibor, stones, tracker, fever, tablets, surgery, monocular, held map, rail halts, trig points, save and load | A whole session without missions works |\n| 6 Story | Mission runner, dialogue, voices, buddies, rescues, M0 to End, Ledger, endings. Playthrough suite | A bot and you both finish it |\n| 7 Shell | Title, all menus, settings, glyph sets, About, touch gate, attract, dev mode | Every screen works by pad, keyboard and mouse |\n| 8 Multiplayer | Sim/view puppets, host, client, sessions, Cash Run, card, solo bots, link | Hub and link suites pass with a real round |\n| 9 Polish | All music, ambience, feel, art passes, balance with the sliders, screenshots | You'd show it to someone |\n| 10 Ship | Final build, About pages, exit interview, chat reply, `node tests/run.mjs --all` | Section 27 is all true |\n\n---\n\n## 26. Cut order\n\nIf you can't finish everything, cut whole things from the top of this list. Don't leave stubs, and remove all traces (menu entries, map marks, lines). Keep every feature in the demo reachable and shown.\n\n1. Fauna (vultures first).\n2. Same-computer link (keep hub and solo).\n3. The game's own hub card (use the hub's card: `card:false`).\n4. Chase camera; dust weather.\n5. Mercy Runs after the first; trig points down to 3; cases down to 6.\n6. M5 (Mags offers her alternate plan in M6 instead: get the field workers out first, for less pay).\n7. M4 (give the tracker in M3; use the MG in M7; Dov joins at the bar).\n8. M8 (the column just starts walking after M7).\n9. Shared-world → ghost → parallel (section 19).\n\nNever cut: fire, wear and jams, fever, the held map, buddy rescue and the finish-it choice, Harrow's twist, dev mode with sliders, attract mode, glyphs and native mouse, touch gate, the hub check, music at 10%, the voices.\n\n---\n\n## 27. Done, reports, coverage\n\n**Done means:** every line below is true and you've checked it.\n- [ ] Your title, chosen by the brief's procedure, appears on the title screen and in `<title>`.\n- [ ] The one HTML file runs from `file://` with nothing else beside it.\n- [ ] `node tests/run.mjs --all` reports 0 failed.\n- [ ] All four hub scenarios pass, and the game still runs outside a session.\n- [ ] You finished the game yourself by bot, both endings.\n- [ ] No TODOs, placeholders or stubbed features anywhere.\n- [ ] Every screen shows native prompts for pad (PlayStation and Xbox glyphs) and keyboard/mouse.\n- [ ] You looked at the screenshots.\n- [ ] `pixel-engine.js` is byte-identical to the copy in the kit's zip (keep the zip in `vendor/` and compare in the `static` suite).\n\n**About and Credits screen** (in-game, paged, reached from main menu and pause; text in `src/content/about.js`). Your brief marks this as critical. It must show:\n- **Source Information,** with every field your brief lists: Date (from your brief), Source (Far Cry 2), Plan (the file name of this plan as you received it), Genre and Perspective, Tech (engine and its version, three.js r186, Rapier 0.20, esbuild, your additions), Art Direction, Animation, Audio, Online, Testing, Research, Environment, Model (from your brief), and Usage: *added on import*. Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\n- **Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback:** your brief's questions and your honest answers, in order, each on its own page. Don't estimate cost.\n- **Credits:** Pixel Engine (MIT), three.js (MIT), Rapier (Apache-2.0), the AI Hub session client, and \"Inspired by Far Cry 2; not affiliated\".\n\n**Your final chat reply** repeats the same Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback.\n\n**The exit interview file** your brief specifies goes beside the HTML, in the exact JSON shape it gives, every value filled, and must parse. Suggested catalogue values: type `Game`; genre `Shooter`; source `Far Cry 2`; series `Far Cry`; players `1–4`; tags such as `first-person`, `pixel art`, `co-op`, `versus`, `vehicles`, `story`; the name is your title.\n\n**Where each line of your brief is covered:**\n\n| Brief item | Section |\n| --- | --- |\n| Source, original game, capture world, characters, themes, tone | 1, 2, 15 |\n| Genre, perspective | 1 |\n| Title by random pick (left to you) | top, 25 |\n| Research | 3 (done for you; research more if you want) |\n| Single HTML package, CDN allowance, bundle into root | 23 |\n| Engine kit kept as shipped, systems added on top | 3, 4, 23 |\n| Art direction: native base, new assets, library for generic props | 20 |\n| Animation: native base, new animations | 21 |\n| Audio in code, Animalese voices, music 10% | 22 |\n| Online and multiplayer, in the hub and on its own | 19 |\n| Dev subfolder, what not to read, shared ports and processes | 4, 24 |\n| Performance out of scope | 3 |\n| Testing: headless, scripted playthrough, one command, screenshots only when needed, no review subagents | 24 |\n| Effort | Yours to spend; 25 and 26 order it |\n| This computer and its stand-ins | 3, 4, 24 |\n| Feature-complete vertical slice, infrastructure for later build-out | 4, 14, 25 |\n| Dev mode from pause, standard tools, live sliders, reset | 17 |\n| Attract mode at 10 s, any input exits | 18 |\n| Narrative tone | 15 |\n| 10-foot controller first, native keyboard and mouse, hover focus, glyphs, Xbox option | 16 |\n| No dense web-style screens | 16 |\n| Touch-only notice, settings button, attract runs | 16, 18 |\n| Done: no TODOs, placeholders or stubs | top, 26, 27 |\n| Source Information, feedback sections, chat reply, About screen | 27 |\n| Exit interview | 27 |\n","numLines":280,"startLine":850,"totalLines":1129}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014m8qDEoSfvdg3QBqkG9xc2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
