{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Lg17c4pPp8UD1HVQkiJXSn","type":"tool_result","content":"API.md\nASSETS.md\nCHANGELOG.md\nCREDITS.md\nGUIDE.md\nLIBRARY.md\nLICENSE\nREADME.md\ncheck.mjs\nexamples\ngame.js\nindex.html\nlibrary.json\nmanifest.json\npacks\npixel-engine.d.ts\npixel-engine.js\ntypes\nvendor\n  60159 GUIDE.md\n 248164 API.md\n  15883 ASSETS.md\n  57520 CHANGELOG.md\n4864228 pixel-engine.js\n5245954 total\n# Changelog\n\nWhat changed in Pixel Engine for a game built on it, newest first. The version is\n`package.json`'s; a game reads it as `ENGINE_VERSION`, `Engine.version` or\n`engine.state().version`. The engine kit (`npm run bundle`, docs/GUIDE.md) ships this file.\n\nWhen a change alters the public API (`src/bundle.ts` exports) or something a game can see,\nbump the version (minor while it is 0.x) and add its section here; `npm test` fails when\n`package.json`'s version has no section.\n\n## 0.46.0\n\n- **No more handoff page**: the engine's site is gone, so `manifest.json` has no `handoff` and the\n  kit's `README.md` no longer names a page for agents. Newer kits are where they were:\n  `latest` (the newest release's zip), `releases` and `source`.\n\n## 0.45.0\n\n- **The kit runs in Node**: `Engine.headless(game, { assets })` from `pixel-engine.js` alone, with\n  no `node_modules`. In Node, Rapier's wasm comes from the data URL the kit inlines, and a reader","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"feff64bd-df6d-45b2-b337-83604d3a2d73","uuid":"0d407c69-203b-4b6a-955e-8036c61e513a","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:21:05.832Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"API.md\nASSETS.md\nCHANGELOG.md\nCREDITS.md\nGUIDE.md\nLIBRARY.md\nLICENSE\nREADME.md\ncheck.mjs\nexamples\ngame.js\nindex.html\nlibrary.json\nmanifest.json\npacks\npixel-engine.d.ts\npixel-engine.js\ntypes\nvendor\n  60159 GUIDE.md\n 248164 API.md\n  15883 ASSETS.md\n  57520 CHANGELOG.md\n4864228 pixel-engine.js\n5245954 total\n# Changelog\n\nWhat changed in Pixel Engine for a game built on it, newest first. The version is\n`package.json`'s; a game reads it as `ENGINE_VERSION`, `Engine.version` or\n`engine.state().version`. The engine kit (`npm run bundle`, docs/GUIDE.md) ships this file.\n\nWhen a change alters the public API (`src/bundle.ts` exports) or something a game can see,\nbump the version (minor while it is 0.x) and add its section here; `npm test` fails when\n`package.json`'s version has no section.\n\n## 0.46.0\n\n- **No more handoff page**: the engine's site is gone, so `manifest.json` has no `handoff` and the\n  kit's `README.md` no longer names a page for agents. Newer kits are where they were:\n  `latest` (the newest release's zip), `releases` and `source`.\n\n## 0.45.0\n\n- **The kit runs in Node**: `Engine.headless(game, { assets })` from `pixel-engine.js` alone, with\n  no `node_modules`. In Node, Rapier's wasm comes from the data URL the kit inlines, and a reader","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Lg17c4pPp8UD1HVQkiJXSn","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
