{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgkf242XQcqmmesp314yc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01F7487UrtavVDqQuyaW2GVY","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162033__x07393c/work/FarPry2*/ && W=400 tools/api.sh Physics | grep -E \"castRay|tag|trigger|groundBelow|explode|castShape|bind|counts|alpha\" | head -14"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":833,"cache_read_input_tokens":236223,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":833},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"feff64bd-df6d-45b2-b337-83604d3a2d73","uuid":"6ebb3ebf-a01d-409b-bfc3-ae436b658654","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:34:06.915Z","request_id":"req_011Cgkf23m9j36RPECiE1o36","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01F7487UrtavVDqQuyaW2GVY":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162033__x07393c/work/FarPry2*/ && W=400 tools/api.sh Physics | grep -E \"castRay|tag|trigger|groundBelow|explode|castShape|bind|counts|alpha\" | head -14"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F7487UrtavVDqQuyaW2GVY","type":"tool_result","content":"- `alpha: number`: Interpolation factor between the previous and current physics step, 0..1.\n- `onStep(f: () => void, o: { first?: boolean } = {}): () => void`: Run `f` after every fixed step, before bound meshes (`bind`) read their bodies. Listeners run in the order they were added (instanced bodies keep their last two poses, a ragdoll holds its joint limits); `{ first: true }` runs `f` ahead of all of those, for so…\n- `explode(at: readonly [number, number, number] | Vector3, o: ExplosionOptions = {}): number`: Push every dynamic body near `at` away from it (physics/forces.ts). Returns how many.\n- `bind(body: RAPIER.RigidBody, object: Object3D): void`: Make `object` follow `body` (interpolated).\n- `unbind(object: Object3D): void`\n- `tag(collider: RAPIER.Collider, ...tags: string[]): RAPIER.Collider`: Tag a collider with gameplay semantics the character controller understands: 'climbable' (ladders/vines), 'pushable', 'grabbable', 'slippery', 'noLedge', 'character', 'noCamera' (camera rays pass through). Games may add their own.\n- `hasTag(collider: RAPIER.Collider | null | undefined, tag: string): boolean`\n- `castRay(from: Vector3, dir: Vector3, maxDistance: number, ignoreTags: readonly string[] = NO_TAGS, exclude?: RAPIER.RigidBody): { distance: number; collider: RAPIER.Collider; normal: Vector3; point: Vector3 } | null`: Ray cast returning distance, hit collider and surface normal.\n- `groundBelow(origin: Vector3, maxDistance = 20, exclude?: RAPIER.RigidBody): { y: number; distance: number } | null`: Distance straight down from `origin` to the first collider (excluding `exclude`).\n- `trigger(shape: TriggerShape, at: readonly [number, number, number] | Vector3, options: TriggerOptions = {}): Trigger`: A trigger volume with enter/exit callbacks (pickups, checkpoints, kill zones, doors). Checked after every fixed step against dynamic and kinematic bodies (the character included); set `includeStatic` for level geometry. Never blocks movement or rays.\n- `updateTriggers(): void`: Run every trigger's overlap query now (Physics.update does this after each step).\n- `remove(target: RAPIER.RigidBody | RAPIER.Collider): void`: Remove a rigid body (with its colliders and any bound Object3D binding) or a single collider. Removing a collider whose fixed body has no other colliders removes that body too (what `addStaticBox` & co. create). Tags and trigger overlaps are cleaned up.\n- `clear(): void`: Empty the world: every body, collider, joint, character and vehicle controller, trigger, tag, binding, mover, field and belt goes; gravity and the solver's iterations go back to their defaults, the step accumulator and the step count reset. `world` is a new R…\n- `counts(): { bodies: number; colliders: number; joints: number; tags: number; bindings: number; triggers: number; controllers: number; vehicles: number; movers: number; fields: number; belts: number; }`: Sizes of everything Physics tracks (leak checks, debug UI).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"feff64bd-df6d-45b2-b337-83604d3a2d73","uuid":"0ee3d180-ded6-4d5b-b886-a1de89b954f9","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:34:06.933Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"- `alpha: number`: Interpolation factor between the previous and current physics step, 0..1.\n- `onStep(f: () => void, o: { first?: boolean } = {}): () => void`: Run `f` after every fixed step, before bound meshes (`bind`) read their bodies. Listeners run in the order they were added (instanced bodies keep their last two poses, a ragdoll holds its joint limits); `{ first: true }` runs `f` ahead of all of those, for so…\n- `explode(at: readonly [number, number, number] | Vector3, o: ExplosionOptions = {}): number`: Push every dynamic body near `at` away from it (physics/forces.ts). Returns how many.\n- `bind(body: RAPIER.RigidBody, object: Object3D): void`: Make `object` follow `body` (interpolated).\n- `unbind(object: Object3D): void`\n- `tag(collider: RAPIER.Collider, ...tags: string[]): RAPIER.Collider`: Tag a collider with gameplay semantics the character controller understands: 'climbable' (ladders/vines), 'pushable', 'grabbable', 'slippery', 'noLedge', 'character', 'noCamera' (camera rays pass through). Games may add their own.\n- `hasTag(collider: RAPIER.Collider | null | undefined, tag: string): boolean`\n- `castRay(from: Vector3, dir: Vector3, maxDistance: number, ignoreTags: readonly string[] = NO_TAGS, exclude?: RAPIER.RigidBody): { distance: number; collider: RAPIER.Collider; normal: Vector3; point: Vector3 } | null`: Ray cast returning distance, hit collider and surface normal.\n- `groundBelow(origin: Vector3, maxDistance = 20, exclude?: RAPIER.RigidBody): { y: number; distance: number } | null`: Distance straight down from `origin` to the first collider (excluding `exclude`).\n- `trigger(shape: TriggerShape, at: readonly [number, number, number] | Vector3, options: TriggerOptions = {}): Trigger`: A trigger volume with enter/exit callbacks (pickups, checkpoints, kill zones, doors). Checked after every fixed step against dynamic and kinematic bodies (the character included); set `includeStatic` for level geometry. Never blocks movement or rays.\n- `updateTriggers(): void`: Run every trigger's overlap query now (Physics.update does this after each step).\n- `remove(target: RAPIER.RigidBody | RAPIER.Collider): void`: Remove a rigid body (with its colliders and any bound Object3D binding) or a single collider. Removing a collider whose fixed body has no other colliders removes that body too (what `addStaticBox` & co. create). Tags and trigger overlaps are cleaned up.\n- `clear(): void`: Empty the world: every body, collider, joint, character and vehicle controller, trigger, tag, binding, mover, field and belt goes; gravity and the solver's iterations go back to their defaults, the step accumulator and the step count reset. `world` is a new R…\n- `counts(): { bodies: number; colliders: number; joints: number; tags: number; bindings: number; triggers: number; controllers: number; vehicles: number; movers: number; fields: number; belts: number; }`: Sizes of everything Physics tracks (leak checks, debug UI).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01F7487UrtavVDqQuyaW2GVY","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
