{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkfM4BUqrbGQEyEoaLi8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LsL8QhtKuspdW8xTGUTo3C","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162033__x07393c/work/FarPry2*/ && W=260 tools/api.sh SpriteBatch spriteSheet textureDef | head -40; W=200 tools/api.sh LightPool LightRequest LightHandle | head -24"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":370,"cache_read_input_tokens":279779,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":370},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"feff64bd-df6d-45b2-b337-83604d3a2d73","uuid":"67ecd4de-696b-46fb-ac99-cd3a7e8fe3c7","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:38:21.653Z","request_id":"req_011CgkfM3wLvFMJKAqVokWEL","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01LsL8QhtKuspdW8xTGUTo3C":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162033__x07393c/work/FarPry2*/ && W=260 tools/api.sh SpriteBatch spriteSheet textureDef | head -40; W=200 tools/api.sh LightPool LightRequest LightHandle | head -24"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LsL8QhtKuspdW8xTGUTo3C","type":"tool_result","content":"### class SpriteBatch\n\n- `new SpriteBatch(sheet: SpriteSheet, o: { capacity: number })`\n- `readonly sheet: SpriteSheet`\n- `spawn(at: readonly [number, number, number], o: SpriteOptions = {}): number`: A new sprite (its index), or -1 when full.\n- `set(i: number, o: SpriteOptions & { at?: readonly [number, number, number] }): void`: Move or change sprite `i`.\n- `put(i: number, x: number, y: number, z: number, frame?: number, flip?: boolean): void`: `set` without the options object, for many sprites every frame: position, then frame and mirror.\n- `at(i: number): [number, number, number]`: Where sprite `i` stands.\n- `frameOf(i: number): number`: The frame sprite `i` shows.\n- `dispose(): this`: Frees the GPU-related resources allocated by this instance\n\n### spriteSheet()\n\n```ts\nfunction spriteSheet(idOrDef: string | TextureDef, opts: TextureOptions = {}): SpriteSheet\n```\n\nA sprite sheet for `SpriteBatch`: the def's frames left to right in one row, rows stored top\nfirst (`flipY` false, which SpriteBatch reads). Not cached: a SpriteBatch disposes its sheet.\n\n### textureDef()\n\n```ts\nfunction textureDef(def: T): T\n```\n\nReturns the def as written, typed, so tuples and literals don't widen (as `model` does). Not\n`texture`: TSL's `texture()` samples a map, and games import both.\n\n### class LightPool\n\nA fixed pool of point lights shared by many requests (see the file comment). Available\nto games as `ctx.lights` (sized by quality: low 4, medium 8, high 16), or create your\nown with `new LightPool({ size, parent: scene })` and call `update` every frame.\n\n- `new LightPool(options: LightPoolOptions = {})`\n- `readonly group: Group<Object3DEventMap>`\n- `readonly lights: PointLight[]`\n- `get size: number`: Number of real lights (constant unless `resize`d).\n- `request(options: LightRequestOptions = {}): LightHandle`: Ask for a light. Returns a handle to move, recolour or release.\n- `update(dt: number, focus: Vector3, range = 18): void`: Assign lights for this frame. `focus` is what the camera looks at; requests further than `range` + their radius from it are not lit. Call once\n- `clear(): void`: Release every request at once and darken the lights (level unload).\n- `resize(size: number): void`: Change the number of real lights. Every material using lights recompiles once, so do it rarely (a quality change), never per frame.\n- `stats(): LightPoolStats`\n- `describe(): { id: number; name: string; score: number; slot: number; level: number; alive: boolean }[]`: Every live request with its score and slot (debugging, inspectors).\n- `dispose(): void`\n\n### interface LightHandle\n\nA light request. Change it freely; the pool decides whether it currently owns a real light.\n\n- `readonly id: number`\n- `readonly position: Vector3`: World position (mutable; ignored while following).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"feff64bd-df6d-45b2-b337-83604d3a2d73","uuid":"471285bf-61a6-488d-a7a1-3ac115122d0d","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:38:21.681Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"### class SpriteBatch\n\n- `new SpriteBatch(sheet: SpriteSheet, o: { capacity: number })`\n- `readonly sheet: SpriteSheet`\n- `spawn(at: readonly [number, number, number], o: SpriteOptions = {}): number`: A new sprite (its index), or -1 when full.\n- `set(i: number, o: SpriteOptions & { at?: readonly [number, number, number] }): void`: Move or change sprite `i`.\n- `put(i: number, x: number, y: number, z: number, frame?: number, flip?: boolean): void`: `set` without the options object, for many sprites every frame: position, then frame and mirror.\n- `at(i: number): [number, number, number]`: Where sprite `i` stands.\n- `frameOf(i: number): number`: The frame sprite `i` shows.\n- `dispose(): this`: Frees the GPU-related resources allocated by this instance\n\n### spriteSheet()\n\n```ts\nfunction spriteSheet(idOrDef: string | TextureDef, opts: TextureOptions = {}): SpriteSheet\n```\n\nA sprite sheet for `SpriteBatch`: the def's frames left to right in one row, rows stored top\nfirst (`flipY` false, which SpriteBatch reads). Not cached: a SpriteBatch disposes its sheet.\n\n### textureDef()\n\n```ts\nfunction textureDef(def: T): T\n```\n\nReturns the def as written, typed, so tuples and literals don't widen (as `model` does). Not\n`texture`: TSL's `texture()` samples a map, and games import both.\n\n### class LightPool\n\nA fixed pool of point lights shared by many requests (see the file comment). Available\nto games as `ctx.lights` (sized by quality: low 4, medium 8, high 16), or create your\nown with `new LightPool({ size, parent: scene })` and call `update` every frame.\n\n- `new LightPool(options: LightPoolOptions = {})`\n- `readonly group: Group<Object3DEventMap>`\n- `readonly lights: PointLight[]`\n- `get size: number`: Number of real lights (constant unless `resize`d).\n- `request(options: LightRequestOptions = {}): LightHandle`: Ask for a light. Returns a handle to move, recolour or release.\n- `update(dt: number, focus: Vector3, range = 18): void`: Assign lights for this frame. `focus` is what the camera looks at; requests further than `range` + their radius from it are not lit. Call once\n- `clear(): void`: Release every request at once and darken the lights (level unload).\n- `resize(size: number): void`: Change the number of real lights. Every material using lights recompiles once, so do it rarely (a quality change), never per frame.\n- `stats(): LightPoolStats`\n- `describe(): { id: number; name: string; score: number; slot: number; level: number; alive: boolean }[]`: Every live request with its score and slot (debugging, inspectors).\n- `dispose(): void`\n\n### interface LightHandle\n\nA light request. Change it freely; the pool decides whether it currently owns a real light.\n\n- `readonly id: number`\n- `readonly position: Vector3`: World position (mutable; ignored while following).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LsL8QhtKuspdW8xTGUTo3C","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
