{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkfQfJgfbybdswA2PGoe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017zVituBYrDqhWxbBSYskXh","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162033__x07393c/work/FarPry2*/ && W=260 tools/api.sh BehaviorTree bt BtStatus NavGrid | head -50; grep -n \"^### .*Ragdoll\\|^### HERO_RAGDOLL\" API.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5246,"cache_read_input_tokens":283209,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5246},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"feff64bd-df6d-45b2-b337-83604d3a2d73","uuid":"25c79d26-bf20-4fb9-9f1f-5826ad5026d5","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:39:31.335Z","request_id":"req_011CgkfQf14zn9GuxPT4pSfn","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_017zVituBYrDqhWxbBSYskXh":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162033__x07393c/work/FarPry2*/ && W=260 tools/api.sh BehaviorTree bt BtStatus NavGrid | head -50; grep -n \"^### .*Ragdoll\\|^### HERO_RAGDOLL\" API.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017zVituBYrDqhWxbBSYskXh","type":"tool_result","content":"### class BehaviorTree\n\n- `new BehaviorTree(root: BtNode<B>, blackboard: B)`\n- `ticks: number`: Ticks so far.\n- `time: number`: Seconds ticked so far (the sum of every dt).\n- `status: Status | null`\n- `readonly root: BtNode<B>`\n- `readonly blackboard: B`\n- `tick(dt: number): Status`\n- `halt(): void`: Stop everything (a cutscene, a stun): running actions are told to halt.\n- `trace(): TraceRow[]`: Every node depth-first with this tick's answer: for drawing the tree.\n- `activePath(): string[]`: The names down the branch that decided this tick, root first (the last child each node ran that didn't fail).\n\n### bt\n\n```ts\nconst bt: { readonly selector: <B>(name: string, ...children: BtNode<B>[]) => BtNode<B>; readonly sequence: <B>(name: string, ...children: BtNode<B>[]) => BtNode<B>; ... 8 more ...; readonly cooldown: <B>(child: BtNode<...>, seconds: number, name?: string) => \n```\n\nThe builders in one object, for `bt.selector(...)` without importing each.\n\n### type BtStatus\n\n```ts\ntype BtStatus = 'success' | 'failure' | 'running'\n```\n\nBehaviour trees: an agent's decisions as a tree of small nodes, ticked every step. Each tick\na node answers success, failure or running (still at it). Selectors try their children in\npriority order until one doesn't fail; sequences run theirs in order until one doesn't\nsucceed. Both are reactive: every tick starts again from the first child, so a higher\npriority (flee!) takes over at once, and whatever was running below it is halted.\n\n  const tree = new BehaviorTree(\n    selector('root',\n      sequence('flee', condition('scared?', (b) => b.threat < 3), action('run away', fleeStep)),\n      seq…\n\n### class NavGrid\n\n- `new NavGrid(width: number, height: number, o: NavGridOptions = {})`\n- `static fromRows(rows: readonly string[], o: NavGridOptions & { blocked?: string } = {}): NavGrid`: From an ASCII map: `blocked` characters are closed, everything else open. Default '# ': walls and pits (a ' ' has no floor in RoomKit's maps); past the end of\n- `readonly width: number`\n- `readonly height: number`\n- `readonly cell: number`\n- `readonly ox: number`: World x, z of cell (0, 0)'s corner.\n- `readonly oz: number`\n- `readonly open: Uint8Array`: 1 = walkable.\n- `version: number`: Bumped by `setOpen`: flow fields rebuild.\n- `flowBuilds: number`: How many times a flow field was built (tools: should be one per target cell change).\n1834:### class Ragdoll\n1851:### interface RagdollOptions\n1858:### interface RagdollPart\n3866:### HERO_RAGDOLL","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"feff64bd-df6d-45b2-b337-83604d3a2d73","uuid":"8a776bfa-5536-4d3c-b36e-7f9c9b745886","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:39:31.359Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"### class BehaviorTree\n\n- `new BehaviorTree(root: BtNode<B>, blackboard: B)`\n- `ticks: number`: Ticks so far.\n- `time: number`: Seconds ticked so far (the sum of every dt).\n- `status: Status | null`\n- `readonly root: BtNode<B>`\n- `readonly blackboard: B`\n- `tick(dt: number): Status`\n- `halt(): void`: Stop everything (a cutscene, a stun): running actions are told to halt.\n- `trace(): TraceRow[]`: Every node depth-first with this tick's answer: for drawing the tree.\n- `activePath(): string[]`: The names down the branch that decided this tick, root first (the last child each node ran that didn't fail).\n\n### bt\n\n```ts\nconst bt: { readonly selector: <B>(name: string, ...children: BtNode<B>[]) => BtNode<B>; readonly sequence: <B>(name: string, ...children: BtNode<B>[]) => BtNode<B>; ... 8 more ...; readonly cooldown: <B>(child: BtNode<...>, seconds: number, name?: string) => \n```\n\nThe builders in one object, for `bt.selector(...)` without importing each.\n\n### type BtStatus\n\n```ts\ntype BtStatus = 'success' | 'failure' | 'running'\n```\n\nBehaviour trees: an agent's decisions as a