{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkfzjMTxa7SFtYov4C7n","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YMqaFKx6i17SBaxrvsEPNv","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162033__x07393c/work/FarPry2*/ && W=260 tools/api.sh PlayerSettings Settings | head -40; W=200 tools/api.sh VolumeChannel AudioSettings | head"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2535,"cache_read_input_tokens":354606,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2535},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"feff64bd-df6d-45b2-b337-83604d3a2d73","uuid":"83f9acd7-c4e9-4637-a3ef-d517106c1ad9","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:47:02.070Z","request_id":"req_011Cgkfzj2rik6RLU5wEMojq","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01YMqaFKx6i17SBaxrvsEPNv":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162033__x07393c/work/FarPry2*/ && W=260 tools/api.sh PlayerSettings Settings | head -40; W=200 tools/api.sh VolumeChannel AudioSettings | head"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YMqaFKx6i17SBaxrvsEPNv","type":"tool_result","content":"### interface PlayerSettings\n\nThe player's settings: the standard picture and engine options every game gets, as plain data\n(sound is the AudioManager's, which keeps its own volumes). A field left out is the game's own\nchoice; a field set is the player's and wins over it. `engine.settings` holds them, applies\nthem, saves them per game and shows them in the settings panel (the ⚙ button).\n\n- `look?: string`: A LOOK_PRESETS name. Left out: the look the game gives each level.\n- `pixelArt?: boolean`: Pixel art (the pixel pass), or false for smooth 3D (render mode `raw`).\n- `pixelSize?: 'fine' | 'chunky'`: The art resolution: `fine` (the game's, 480×270 by default) or `chunky` (two thirds of it: bigger pixels).\n- `quality?: QualityOption`: Shadow and light quality: a level, or `auto` (the device's).\n- `fps?: number`: Frame cap: 60, 30, or 0 for the display's own rate.\n- `debugInfo?: boolean`: The debug panel: frame rate, camera, GPU errors and the game's status.\n\n### class Settings\n\n`engine.settings`: the player's settings, applied to the engine and saved. A field the page URL\nsets (`?look=`, `?mode=`, `?res=`, `?quality=`, `?fps=`, `?debug=`: review flags) wins over a\nsaved one at start (which stays saved). `open`, `close` and `toggle` show and hide the\nsettings panel.\n\n- `new Settings(host: SettingsHost, key: string | null)`\n- `readonly key: string | null`\n- `get values: Readonly<PlayerSettings>`: The player's choices in effect: fields left out are the game's (or a review flag's).\n- `get isOpen: boolean`\n- `set(patch: PlayerSettings): void`: Change some settings: applied at once and saved. A field set to `undefined` goes back to the game's.\n- `reset(): void`: Forget every choice, the held ones too: the game's own picture again.\n- `replace(values: PlayerSettings): void`: Make `values` the settings, changing only the fields that differ: the ones it leaves out go back to the game's.\n- `onChange(fn: (values: Readonly<PlayerSettings>) => void): () => void`: Called with the values after every change; returns the unsubscribe.\n- `open(): void`\n- `close(): void`\n- `toggle(): void`\n\n### type VolumeChannel\n\n```ts\ntype VolumeChannel = 'master' | 'sfx' | 'music'\n```\n\n### interface AudioSettings\n\n- `master: number`\n- `sfx: number`","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"feff64bd-df6d-45b2-b337-83604d3a2d73","uuid":"f0a5fc2f-c541-4a1f-8b8e-db403a9df836","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:47:02.095Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"### interface PlayerSettings\n\nThe player's settings: the standard picture and engine options every game gets, as plain data\n(sound is the AudioManager's, which keeps its own volumes). A field left out is the game's own\nchoice; a field set is the player's and wins over it. `engine.settings` holds them, applies\nthem, saves them per game and shows them in the settings panel (the ⚙ button).\n\n- `look?: string`: A LOOK_PRESETS name. Left out: the look the game gives each level.\n- `pixelArt?: boolean`: Pixel art (the pixel pass), or false for smooth 3D (render mode `raw`).\n- `pixelSize?: 'fine' | 'chunky'`: The art resolution: `fine` (the game's, 480×270 by default) or `chunky` (two thirds of it: bigger pixels).\n- `quality?: QualityOption`: Shadow and light quality: a level, or `auto` (the device's).\n- `fps?: number`: Frame cap: 60, 30, or 0 for the display's own rate.\n- `debugInfo?: boolean`: The debug panel: frame rate, camera, GPU errors and the game's status.\n\n### class Settings\n\n`engine.settings`: the player's settings, applied to the engine and saved. A field the page URL\nsets (`?look=`, `?mode=`, `?res=`, `?quality=`, `?fps=`, `?debug=`: review flags) wins over a\nsaved one at start (which stays saved). `open`, `close` and `toggle` show and hide the\nsettings panel.\n\n- `new Settings(host: SettingsHost, key: string | null)`\n- `readonly key: string | null`\n- `get values: Readonly<PlayerSettings>`: The player's choices in effect: fields left out are the game's (or a review flag's).\n- `get isOpen: boolean`\n- `set(patch: PlayerSettings): void`: Change some settings: applied at once and saved. A field set to `undefined` goes back to the game's.\n- `reset(): void`: Forget every choice, the held ones too: the game's own picture again.\n- `replace(values: PlayerSettings): void`: Make `values` the settings, changing only the fields that differ: the ones it leaves out go back to the game's.\n- `onChange(fn: (values: Readonly<PlayerSettings>) => void): () => void`: Called with the values after every change; returns the unsubscribe.\n- `open(): void`\n- `close(): void`\n- `toggle(): void`\n\n### type VolumeChannel\n\n```ts\ntype VolumeChannel = 'master' | 'sfx' | 'music'\n```\n\n### interface AudioSettings\n\n- `master: number`\n- `sfx: number`","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01YMqaFKx6i17SBaxrvsEPNv","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
