{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkmbtSiQTRAsx2H7Q3mZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DNm1XrNtvVtir8VHZsLih9","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162033__x07393c/work/FarPry2*/ && cat > src/content/feedback.js <<'EOF'\n// Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback: the brief's questions with honest answers. Shown on About pages, in the exit interview and the chat reply.\nexport const FEEDBACK = {\n  testing: [\n    ['How many issues did testing catch?', '15 logged in tests/ISSUES.md, plus a few small ones fixed on the spot.'],\n    ['How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?', '9 of the 15.'],\n    ['What was the most helpful test you ran?', 'The scripted playthrough: a bot plays M0 to both endings through the real key, mouse and hold-to-use input, with different choices in two runs. It exposed the frozen AI positions, the Rapier panic and the broken mission wiring that no unit test saw.'],\n    ['What was the least helpful test you ran?', 'The attract-mode run: it proves the tour loops without errors but cannot say whether any beat looks right; only screenshots can, and software rendering shows about one frame a second.'],\n  ],\n  engine: [\n    ['What did you like most about the engine?', 'Engine.headless with step(): fast, repeatable play in Node, and models, textures and sounds as plain data that a sheets tool and renderSound can check without a display. The pixel pipeline makes everything look like one game at once.'],\n    ['Did you get stuck or guess wrong?', 'Yes: Node read pixel-engine.js as CommonJS until package.json said type module; CharacterController.feet returns a fresh vector, not a live one, so my AI froze; removing a controller body with physics.remove panics Rapier; the headless camera is not first person unless asked.'],\n    ['What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?', 'Everything that makes it a game: the 5 m fire grid and its look, first-person hands and wear and jams, soldier AI, the mission and dialogue runner, the screen and prompt system, and the Cash Run netcode.'],\n    ['What was the hardest part about using the engine?', 'First person and menus: replacing the rig step, owning pointer lock, a HUD with only a 5x7 font, and judging a 3D scene at one frame a second without being able to watch it move.'],\n    ['What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)', 'none'],\n    ['If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?', 'Give CharacterController a documented dispose and a live feet vector, so characters can be retired and read safely.'],\n  ],\n  prompt: [\n    ['What did you like most about this prompt?', 'The plan decided what to build and listed verified engine traps, so effort went into building; the cut order and the done list kept scope honest.'],\n    ['What was confusing?', 'How much a single run can finish: the plan is a whole game plus multiplayer, attract mode and dev mode, and some rules pull against each other, such as six items a screen against twenty balance sliders.'],\n    ['What was the hardest thing to do?', 'Breadth: keeping nine systems consistent while every check ran headless, and proving the story could be finished by a bot.'],\n    ['What would you change in this prompt?', 'Name a minimum bar and a budget, and say which cuts are acceptable up front; split the plan into milestones with their own done lists.'],\n  ],\n};\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/content/about.js'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"  { title: 'Credits',\",\"\"\"  { title: 'What this demo leaves out', rows: [['Cut, in the plan\\\\'s order', 'fauna and vultures; the same-computer link; the game\\\\'s own hub card (the hub\\\\'s card is used); dust weather; missions M4 Seed Money, M5 The Water Question and M8 Last Train (the tracker comes with M3, Dov joins at the bar, the column starts walking after M7)'], ['Kept', 'fire, wear and jams, fever, the held map, buddy rescue and Finish It, the twist, dev mode with sliders, attract mode, glyphs and native mouse, the touch gate, the hub check, music at 10 percent, voices']] },\n  { title: 'Credits',\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncat > tools/exit-interview.mjs <<'EOF'\n// Writes ../exit-interview.json from the game's own data, then proves it parses.\nimport { writeFileSync, readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { dirname, resolve } from 'node:path';\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\nimport { SOURCE_INFO } from '../src/content/about.js';\nimport { FEEDBACK } from '../src/content/feedback.js';\nconst root = resolve(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '..');\nconst a = (l) => l.map(([, ans]) => ans);\nconst o = {\n  sourceInformation: { date: SOURCE_INFO.date, source: SOURCE_INFO.source, plan: SOURCE_INFO.plan, genre: SOURCE_INFO.genre, perspective: SOURCE_INFO.perspective, tech: SOURCE_INFO.tech, artDirection: SOURCE_INFO.artDirection, animation: SOURCE_INFO.animation, audio: SOURCE_INFO.audio, online: SOURCE_INFO.online, testing: SOURCE_INFO.testing, research: SOURCE_INFO.research, environment: SOURCE_INFO.environment, model: SOURCE_INFO.model, usage: 'added on import' },\n  testingFeedback: a(FEEDBACK.testing), engineFeedback: a(FEEDBACK.engine), promptFeedback: a(FEEDBACK.prompt),\n  aiHub: { name: 'Far Pry 2', tagline: 'Everything fails. The grass remembers.', description: 'An original first-person war-zone survival shooter: guns that rust and jam, a fever on a timetable, grass fires that follow the wind, three friends for hire and a map that turns out to be the plot. Includes the Cash Run shared-world mode for 1 to 4 players.', type: 'Game', genre: 'Shooter', source: 'Far Cry 2', series: 'Far Cry', players: '1–4',\n    controls: 'Pad: sticks move and look, R2 fire, L2 aim, Square use or reload, L1 heal, D-pad up map. Keyboard and mouse: WASD, mouse, LMB fire, RMB aim, E use, R reload, Q heal, M map.', tags: ['first-person', 'pixel art', 'co-op', 'versus', 'vehicles', 'story'] },\n};\nconst path = resolve(root, '..', 'exit-interview.json');\nwriteFileSync(path, JSON.stringify(o, null, 2) + '\\n'); JSON.parse(readFileSync(path, 'utf8')); console.log('wrote', path);\nEOF\nnode tools/exit-interview.mjs; cat scratch/all.txt | tail -5 | cut -c1-300"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":286,"cache_read_input_tokens":626099,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":286},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"feff64bd-df6d-45b2-b337-83604d3a2d73","uuid":"3aa5b0cf-870c-45f4-9f0e-4c7665c19666","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:00:47.504Z","request_id":"req_011Cgkmbt78P4r6Zt7Nu1ceF","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01DNm1XrNtvVtir8VHZsLih9":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162033__x07393c/work/FarPry2*/ && cat > src/content/feedback.js <<'EOF'\n// Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback: the brief's questions with honest answers. Shown on About pages, in the exit interview and the chat reply.\nexport const FEEDBACK = {\n  testing: [\n    ['How many issues did testing catch?', '15 logged in tests/ISSUES.md, plus a few small ones fixed on the spot.'],\n    ['How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?', '9 of the 15.'],\n    ['What was the most helpful test you ran?', 'The scripted playthrough: a bot plays M0 to both endings through the real key, mouse and hold-to-use input, with different choices in two runs. It exposed the frozen AI positions, the Rapier panic and the broken mission wiring that no unit test saw.'],\n    ['What was the least helpful test you ran?', 'The attract-mode run: it proves the tour loops without errors but cannot say whether any beat looks right; only screenshots can, and software rendering shows about one frame a second.'],\n  ],\n  engine: [\n    ['What did you like most about the engine?', 'Engine.headless with step(): fast, repeatable play in Node, and models, textures and sounds as plain data that a sheets tool and renderSound can check without a display. The pixel pipeline makes everything look like one game at once.'],\n    ['Did you get stuck or guess wrong?', 'Yes: Node read pixel-engine.js as CommonJS until package.json said type module; CharacterController.feet returns a fresh vector, not a live one, so my AI froze; removing a controller body with physics.remove panics Rapier; the headless camera is not first person unless asked.'],\n    ['What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?', 'Everything that makes it a game: the 5 m fire grid and its look, first-person hands and wear and jams, soldier AI, the mission and dialogue runner, the screen and prompt system, and the Cash Run netcode.'],\n    ['What was the hardest part about using the engine?', 'First person and menus: replacing the rig step, owning pointer lock, a HUD with only a 5x7 font, and judging a 3D scene at one frame a second without being able to watch it move.'],\n    ['What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)', 'none'],\n    ['If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?', 'Give CharacterController a documented dispose and a live feet vector, so characters can be retired and read safely.'],\n  ],\n  prompt: [\n    ['What did you like most about this prompt?', 'The plan decided what to build and listed verified engine traps, so effort went into building; the cut order and the done list kept scope honest.'],\n    ['What was confusing?', 'How much a single run can finish: the plan is a whole game plus multiplayer, attract mode and dev mode, and some rules pull against each other, such as six items a screen against twenty balance sliders.'],\n    ['What was the hardest thing to do?', 'Breadth: keeping nine systems consistent while every check ran headless, and proving the story could be finished by a bot.'],\n    ['What would you change in this prompt?', 'Name a minimum bar and a budget, and say which cuts are acceptable up front; split the plan into milestones with their own done lists.'],\n  ],\n};\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/content/about.js'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"  { title: 'Credits',\",\"\"\"  { title: 'What this demo leaves out', rows: [['Cut, in the plan\\\\'s order', 'fauna and vultures; the same-computer link; the game\\\\'s own hub card (the hub\\\\'s card is used); dust weather; missions M4 Seed Money, M5 The Water Question and M8 Last Train (the tracker comes with M3, Dov joins at the bar, the column starts walking after M7)'], ['Kept', 'fire, wear and jams, fever, the held map, buddy rescue and Finish It, the twist, dev mode with sliders, attract mode, glyphs and native mouse, the touch gate, the hub check, music at 10 percent, voices']] },\n  { title: 'Credits',\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncat > tools/exit-interview.mjs <<'EOF'\n// Writes ../exit-interview.json from the game's own data, then proves it parses.\nimport { writeFileSync, readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { dirname, resolve } from 'node:path';\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\nimport { SOURCE_INFO } from '../src/content/about.js';\nimport { FEEDBACK } from '../src/content/feedback.js';\nconst root = resolve(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '..');\nconst a = (l) => l.map(([, ans]) => ans);\nconst o = {\n  sourceInformation: { date: SOURCE_INFO.date, source: SOURCE_INFO.source, plan: SOURCE_INFO.plan, genre: SOURCE_INFO.genre, perspective: SOURCE_INFO.perspective, tech: SOURCE_INFO.tech, artDirection: SOURCE_INFO.artDirection, animation: SOURCE_INFO.animation, audio: SOURCE_INFO.audio, online: SOURCE_INFO.online, testing: SOURCE_INFO.testing, research: SOURCE_INFO.research, environment: SOURCE_INFO.environment, model: SOURCE_INFO.model, usage: 'added on import' },\n  testingFeedback: a(FEEDBACK.testing), engineFeedback: a(FEEDBACK.engine), promptFeedback: a(FEEDBACK.prompt),\n  aiHub: { name: 'Far Pry 2', tagline: 'Everything fails. The grass remembers.', description: 'An original first-person war-zone survival shooter: guns that rust and jam, a fever on a timetable, grass fires that follow the wind, three friends for hire and a map that turns out to be the plot. Includes the Cash Run shared-world mode for 1 to 4 players.', type: 'Game', genre: 'Shooter', source: 'Far Cry 2', series: 'Far Cry', players: '1–4',\n    controls: 'Pad: sticks move and look, R2 fire, L2 aim, Square use or reload, L1 heal, D-pad up map. Keyboard and mouse: WASD, mouse, LMB fire, RMB aim, E use, R reload, Q heal, M map.', tags: ['first-person', 'pixel art', 'co-op', 'versus', 'vehicles', 'story'] },\n};\nconst path = resolve(root, '..', 'exit-interview.json');\nwriteFileSync(path, JSON.stringify(o, null, 2) + '\\n'); JSON.parse(readFileSync(path, 'utf8')); console.log('wrote', path);\nEOF\nnode tools/exit-interview.mjs; cat scratch/all.txt | tail -5 | cut -c1-300"}}}
