{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgkp2yUWs9qTyySjN7Cxv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I built **Far Pry 2**, a single-file first-person war-zone survival shooter, but without every mission or feature in PLAN.md. `node tests/run.mjs --all` ends with 1082 passed, 0 failed, covering the static, systems, playthrough, replay, browser and hub suites. A bot plays M0 through to both endings using real key, mouse and hold-to-use input, and all four AI Hub scenarios pass. I opened the real WebGPU build in Chromium and looked at screenshots of the title, the first-person HUD, the night fire, Tibor's rack and the dev-mode sliders. I did not look at the dialogue, surgery, held-map or ending screens, and nothing was playtested by hand.\n\n## What's missing from the plan\nEverything cut comes from the plan's own cut order. The About screen also lists these.\n- **Missions:** M4 Seed Money, M5 The Water Question and M8 Last Train. The tracker now comes with M3, Dov joins at the bar, and the column starts walking after M7. M0, M1, M2, M3, M6, M7, M9 and the ending are all in, plus two extra Mercy Runs.\n- **Cut features:** fauna and vultures, the same-computer link, the game's own hub card (the hub's card is used) and dust weather.\n\n## Files\n- **Game:** `FarPry2-FarCry2-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261105-162033.html`, in the work folder, 5.7 MB, runs from `file://`.\n- **Exit interview:** `exit-interview.json`, in the same folder, parses as JSON.\n- **Dev folder:** `FarPry2-FarCry2-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261105-162033/` holds the source, the tests, `DESIGNERS.md` (how to add content) and `tests/ISSUES.md`.\n- **Title:** \"Far Pry 2\", picked by RNG (index 25 of 50). `PROGRESS.md` is in the work folder.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-05 16:20:33\n- **Source:** Far Cry 2\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** open-world first-person shooter with survival pressure and systemic fire. First person on foot, at the wheel and in story scenes, with an optional chase camera in vehicles.\n- **Tech:** Pixel Engine (riftlight) 0.46.0, three.js r186, Rapier 0.20, esbuild 0.28.2, Playwright 1.63.0 for tests. The game itself is plain JavaScript modules.\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's 3D-as-pixel-art look at 480×270 with toon materials and the 16-colour palette. New models are written as data for people, guns, vehicles and buildings.\n- **Animation:** engine clip data compiled to mixer clips on the hero rig, with lower/upper body layering and ragdolls on death. First-person hands and guns use my own keyframe clips rather than engine clips.\n- **Audio:** all sound is written in code. Effects, music (default volume 10%) and Animalese-style voices, with no audio files.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1 in shared-world mode, 1 to 4 players (Cash Run). Solo with hired guns also works.\n- **Testing:** headless Node suites plus Playwright Chromium on `file://` and the four hub harness scenarios. No review subagents.\n- **Research:** the supplied plan, the engine kit's guide and API docs, and the AI Hub README. Nothing else.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** added on import\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** 15 are logged in `tests/ISSUES.md`, plus a few small ones fixed on the spot.\n- **How many were critical?** 9 of the 15.\n- **Most helpful test?** The scripted playthrough, which plays M0 to both endings with different choices in two runs. It exposed the frozen AI positions, a Rapier panic and broken mission wiring that no unit test saw.\n- **Least helpful test?** The attract-mode run. It shows the tour loops without errors but can't tell whether any beat looks right.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** `Engine.headless` with `step()` for fast, repeatable play in Node, and models, textures and sounds as plain data that can be checked without a display.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:**\n  - Node read `pixel-engine.js` as CommonJS until `package.json` said `\"type\": \"module\"`.\n  - `CharacterController.feet` returns a fresh vector rather than a live one, so every AI froze in place.\n  - Removing a controller's body panics Rapier.\n  - The headless camera isn't first-person unless you ask.\n- **Had to build myself:** the fire grid, first-person hands and wear and jams, soldier AI, the mission and dialogue runner, the screens and prompts, and the Cash Run netcode.\n- **Hardest part:** first-person camera and pointer-lock handling, a HUD with only a 5×7 font, and judging a 3D scene at one frame a second.\n- **Changed in the engine:** none.\n- **One change I'd make:** give `CharacterController` a documented dispose and a live `feet` vector.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the plan decided what to build and listed verified engine traps, so effort went into building. The cut order and done list kept scope honest.\n- **Confusing:** how much one run can finish, and some rules that pull against each other, such as six items a screen against twenty balance sliders.\n- **Hardest:** breadth, keeping nine systems consistent while every check ran headless and proving a bot could finish the story.\n- **Would change:** name a minimum bar and a budget, say up front which cuts are acceptable, and split the plan into milestones with their own done lists.\n\nThe same text is on the in-game About and Credits pages."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":829,"cache_read_input_tokens":662706,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":829},"output_tokens":836,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"feff64bd-df6d-45b2-b337-83604d3a2d73","uuid":"b3224cc1-43ed-408f-b8d8-fecad9799ac1","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:32:26.075Z","request_id":"req_011Cgkp2yCPfQZzLbLKG17Eh"}
